EXAM_DATA.papers["2012-english-one"] = {"id":"2012-english-one","year":2012,"label":"2012 英语一","era":"modern","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2012-english-one/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"estimated","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"The ethical judgments of the Supreme Court justices have become an important issue recently. The court cannot   {{1}}   its legitimacy as guardian of the rule of law   {{2}}   justices behave like politicians. Yet, in several instances, justices acted in ways that   {{3}}   the court's reputation for being independent and impartial."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"Justice Antonin Scalia, for example, appeared at political events. That kind of activity makes it less likely that the court's decisions will be   {{4}}   as impartial judgments. Part of the problem is that the justices are not   {{5}}   by an ethics code. At the very least, the court should make itself   {{6}}   to the code of conduct that   {{7}}   to the rest of the federal judiciary."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"This and other similar cases   {{8}}   the question of whether there is still a   {{9}}   between the court and politics."},{"id":"p-section1-4","text":"The framers of the Constitution envisioned law   {{10}}   having authority apart from politics. They gave justices permanent positions   {{11}}   they would be free to   {{12}}   those in power and have no need to   {{13}}   political support. Our legal system was designed to set law apart from politics precisely because they are so closely   {{14}}   ."},{"id":"p-section1-5","text":"Constitutional law is political because it results from choices rooted in fundamental social   {{15}}   like liberty and property. When the court deals with social policy decisions, the law it   {{16}}   is inescapably political – which is why decisions split along ideological lines are so easily   {{17}}   as unjust."},{"id":"p-section1-6","text":"The justices must   {{18}}   doubts about the court's legitimacy by making themselves   {{19}}   to the code of conduct. That would make rulings more likely to be seen as separate from politics and,   {{20}}   , convincing as law."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"emphasize"},{"key":"B","text":"maintain"},{"key":"C","text":"modify"},{"key":"D","text":"recognize"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"1.","reason":"本段标题句＋下文\"损害声誉\"反向印证 本句框架是 The court cannot __(1)__ its legitimacy as guardian of the rule of law __(2)__ justices behave like politicians.，紧跟着的 justices acted in ways that __(3)__ the court's reputation for being independent and impartial 说明\"行为像政客\"会\"削弱声誉\"。反过来推：法院\"无法保住/维持\"其合法性。线索指向\"保持、维系\"这一语义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"emphasize 是\"强调\"，强调合法性并不等于\"保住\"合法性；句意要求的是法院\"在何种条件下能继续拥有\"合法性，不是\"强调\"它。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"maintain 与 legitimacy 构成高频搭配 maintain legitimacy（维持合法性），完全契合\"若大法官行为像政客，法院就无法保住其合法性\"的因果逻辑，与下文 reputation 的\"声誉\"链条同向。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"modify 指\"修改、调整\"，合法性这种属性不是被\"修改\"的对象，搭配不当。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"recognize 是\"承认、认识到\"，是外界对法院合法性的态度；这里主语是 the court（法院自己），不可能\"自己承认自己的合法性\"。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"when"},{"key":"B","text":"lest"},{"key":"C","text":"before"},{"key":"D","text":"unless"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"2.","reason":"主句否定 + 从句条件构成\"在……之时不能\" 本句 That kind of activity makes it less likely that the court's decisions will be __(4)__ as impartial judgments. 与下文 Scalia 出席政治活动的例证一起证实：当 justices behave like politicians 时，法院无法维系合法性。即\"在大法官像政客行事的时候\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"when 引导时间状语，\"当大法官行为像政客时，法院无法维持合法性\"，与下文 P2 列举 Scalia 在政治场合露面的情景吻合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"lest 意为\"以免、唯恐\"，搭配的是\"防止某种坏事发生\"的语义，且通常要求虚拟语气；这里主句已是 cannot maintain，再说\"以免大法官像政客\"语义自相矛盾。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"before 表示\"在……之前\"，但本句不是\"在政客化之前法院就失去了合法性\"，时间逻辑错位。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"unless 是\"除非\"。主句 cannot maintain 已是否定，再用 unless 等于\"除非大法官像政客，否则就无法维持合法性\"——彻底反了。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"restored"},{"key":"B","text":"weakened"},{"key":"C","text":"established"},{"key":"D","text":"eliminated"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"Yet 转折＋\"impartial 反面\"反向锁定贬义 本句 Yet, in several instances, justices acted in ways that __(3)__ the court's reputation for being independent and impartial. 句首 Yet 与上句 The court cannot __(1)__ its legitimacy as guardian of the rule of law __(2)__ justices behave like politicians. 形成转折，意思是\"然而大法官的某些行为伤害了独立、公正的声誉\"。线索指向\"贬义、削弱\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"restored 表\"恢复\"，与 Yet 的转折逻辑相反——前文若呼吁维系合法性，转折后应是\"损害\"。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"weakened 即\"削弱\"，与 Yet 的转折语气、\"以政客方式行事\"的行为后果完全契合。weaken one's reputation 也是地道搭配。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"established 是\"建立\"，意味着声誉本不存在——与 the court's reputation（既有的声誉）冲突。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"eliminated 表\"彻底清除\"，几次 instances（实例）远不至于\"彻底消除\"法院声誉，程度严重过头。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"challenged"},{"key":"B","text":"compromised"},{"key":"C","text":"suspected"},{"key":"D","text":"accepted"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"4.","reason":"本句即可定的搭配，并由 less likely 反向锁定 That kind of activity makes it less likely that the court's decisions will be __(4)__ as impartial judgments. 关键在 makes it less likely——\"使……不太可能\"。被填动词要表达\"被人们视/接受为公正判决\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"challenged 与 as 搭配少见，\"被挑战为公正判决\"语义不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"compromised 意为\"妥协、有损\"，be compromised as 不构成正常搭配，且\"被有损为公正判决\"语义不通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"suspected 后接 as 通常带负面对象（suspected as a spy）；与 impartial judgments（正面对象）搭配反向。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"accepted 与 as 构成 be accepted as（被认作/被接受为），\"裁决不太可能被接受为公正判决\"贴合\"政治活动→公信力受损\"链条。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"advanced"},{"key":"B","text":"caught"},{"key":"C","text":"bound"},{"key":"D","text":"founded"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"5.","reason":"下文呼吁 subject to the code of conduct 是同指改述 At the very least, the court should make itself __(6)__ to the code of conduct that __(7)__ to the rest of the federal judiciary. 与本句构成同义改述：被填动词的语义应等同于 subject/bound（受约束）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"advanced 是\"推进、提出\"，be advanced by a code 不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"caught 表\"抓住\"，与 ethics code 搭配毫无意义。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"bound 与 by 构成 be bound by（受……约束），\"大法官不受伦理守则约束\"恰好对应下文应承担守则的对策。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"founded 表\"创立\"，be founded by 通常指公司、组织被某人创立，与 the justices 不匹配。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"resistant"},{"key":"B","text":"subject"},{"key":"C","text":"immune"},{"key":"D","text":"prone"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"6.","reason":"与上空 bound 同指 + 下文 code of conduct 本句紧接上文 the justices are not __(5)__ by an ethics code，是\"问题→对策\"的对策侧；同时再次呼应 P6 的 making themselves __(19)__ to the code of conduct，三处构成同义链。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"resistant 是\"抗拒……的\"，be resistant to 表\"抗拒\"，与作者呼吁\"接受守则\"的语义相反。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"subject 与 to 构成 be subject to（受……约束/服从于）；make itself subject to the code of conduct 即\"使自己受守则约束\"，与作者主张完全吻合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"immune 表\"不受影响、豁免\"，be immune to=\"对……免疫\"，与\"接受约束\"语义反向。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"prone 是 be prone to=\"易于、倾向于\"，后接的多是负面后果（prone to errors），与\"行为守则\"不搭。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"resorts"},{"key":"B","text":"sticks"},{"key":"C","text":"leads"},{"key":"D","text":"applies"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"7.","reason":"主语 code of conduct + 对象 federal judiciary 即\"规则适用于司法机构\" 本句主语是 the code of conduct（行为守则），to 后是 the rest of the federal judiciary（其余联邦司法机构），逻辑只能是\"该守则适用于其余联邦司法机构\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"resorts 与 to 构成 resort to（诉诸、求助于），主语通常是人/机构，不是规则本身。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"sticks 与 to 构成 stick to（坚持、固守），主语应是\"遵守者\"，而非\"被遵守的规则\"。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"leads 与 to 构成 lead to（导致），\"行为守则导致其余司法机构\"语义荒谬。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"applies 与 to 构成 apply to（适用于），\"该行为守则适用于其余联邦司法机构\"完全自然。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"evade"},{"key":"B","text":"raise"},{"key":"C","text":"deny"},{"key":"D","text":"settle"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"8.","reason":"句中 This and other similar cases 是引子，后接的是一个疑问 句子结构是\"这些案例引出/提出 + 是否还有界线 的问题\"。whether there is still a __(9)__ between the court and politics 是问题内容，本句基调是\"提出问题\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"evade 是\"回避\"，案例本身不会回避问题，回避的应是当事人。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"raise 与 the question 搭配自然，This and other similar cases __(8)__ the question of——\"这些案例引出了……的问题\"。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"deny 是\"否认\"，否认一个问题语义不通，且与后文\"是否还有界线\"的开放疑问基调相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"settle 是\"解决\"，与下文留下的开放疑问 whether there is still a __(9)__ between the court and politics 矛盾。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"line"},{"key":"B","text":"barrier"},{"key":"C","text":"similarity"},{"key":"D","text":"conflict"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"下段制宪意图\"司法与政治分开\"是关键同指 The framers of the Constitution envisioned law __(10)__ having authority apart from politics. 与 Our legal system was designed to set law apart from politics precisely because they are so closely __(14)__. 表明\"司法与政治应分开\"。所以\"两者之间\"应是\"界线\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"line 指\"界线、分界\"，draw a line between 是常用语；对应 set law apart from politics 的\"分开\"含义最贴。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"barrier 是\"壁垒、屏障\"，语气过强；文章不是说要在司法与政治之间筑墙，而是讨论它们\"是否仍有分界\"。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"similarity 表\"相似\"，与作者\"应分开\"的立场反向。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"conflict 是\"冲突\"，本文焦点是\"是否还有界线\"而非\"是否冲突\"；且\"冲突\"本身不构成\"分开\"的同义表达。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"by"},{"key":"B","text":"as"},{"key":"C","text":"through"},{"key":"D","text":"towards"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"语法形态","stemZh":"10.","reason":"envision … as having 的固定句式 envisioned law __(10)__ having authority 本身就指向 envision sth as doing sth=\"把……设想为做某事\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"by 不是 envision 的固定介词搭配，\"通过具有权威\"语义不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"as 构成 envision sth as doing sth，\"将法律设想为具有独立于政治的权威\"，最准确表达了制宪者的设想。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"through 表\"穿过、通过\"，与 envision 不搭配。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"towards 表方向，与 envision 后接\"被设想为何\"的语义不对位。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"so"},{"key":"B","text":"since"},{"key":"C","text":"provided"},{"key":"D","text":"though"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"11.","reason":"\"赋终身职→使其能独立\"是目的关系 主句 They gave justices permanent positions 与从句 they would be free to __(12)__ those in power 是\"制度安排→预期目的\"链条；so + 从句即\"以便\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"so 引导目的状语，\"赋予终身职位以便他们能自由地……\"，承上启下。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"since 是\"既然/因为\"，\"因为他们能自由地……，所以给终身职\"颠倒了因果。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"provided 表\"只要、如果\"，把目的关系硬扭成条件关系。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"though 是\"尽管\"，主从句无让步意味。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"serve"},{"key":"B","text":"satisfy"},{"key":"C","text":"upset"},{"key":"D","text":"replace"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"12.","reason":"free to + 动词、与下空\"无需迎合政治支持\"并列 they would be free to __(12)__ those in power and have no need to __(13)__ political support. 两个并列动作描绘\"独立\"——独立体现在\"敢于对抗权贵\"且\"不必经营政治支持\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"serve 是\"服务\"，与\"独立、敢于对抗\"反向。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"satisfy 表\"满足、取悦\"，与下句\"不必迎合政治支持\"反向。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"upset 是\"使不安、扰乱\"，free to upset those in power=\"能自由地触怒/挑战权贵\"，恰是 \"司法独立\"的具象表现。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"replace 是\"取代\"，司法不应取代行政权力，越界。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"confirm"},{"key":"B","text":"express"},{"key":"C","text":"cultivate"},{"key":"D","text":"offer"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"13.","reason":"have no need to + 动词 与上文\"独立\"主题对应 have no need to __(13)__ political support 与\"自由对抗权贵\"并列；\"无需……政治支持\"的动作应是政客对支持的常规动作——经营、培植。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"confirm 是\"确认\"，confirm political support 不构成正常表达。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"express 是\"表达\"，应是支持者表达支持，不是被支持者表达。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"cultivate 与 support 搭配自然且形象，\"大法官无需经营政治支持\"贴合本段独立性主题。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"offer 是\"提供\"，应是大法官接受支持，而非提供支持。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"guarded"},{"key":"B","text":"followed"},{"key":"C","text":"studied"},{"key":"D","text":"tied"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"14.","reason":"precisely because they are so closely ___ 是反讽式因果 Our legal system was designed to set law apart from politics precisely because they are so closely __(14)__. 全句意思是\"正因为它们如此紧密交织，制度上才要刻意把它们分开\"——这里要的是\"紧密相连/纠缠\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"guarded 是\"被守卫\"，无法表达\"两者紧密相连\"。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"followed 表\"被跟随\"，与 closely 搭配可成 closely followed，但表示\"被密切关注\"，与\"两者关系紧密\"不同。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"studied 是\"被研究\"，与\"法律和政治本质上紧密关联\"无关。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"tied 与 closely 构成 closely tied（紧密关联），完美承载\"两者本就紧密相连，故立法刻意切开\"的反差。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"concepts"},{"key":"B","text":"theories"},{"key":"C","text":"divisions"},{"key":"D","text":"conventions"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"15.","reason":"like liberty and property 是例证锚点 choices rooted in fundamental social __(15)__ like liberty and property. 中 liberty 和 property 是抽象观念，最自然的上位词是\"基本社会观念/概念\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"concepts 表\"概念、观念\"，liberty 和 property 是典型的基本社会观念，匹配最佳。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"theories 表\"理论\"，liberty 和 property 不是\"理论\"，是观念本身。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"divisions 表\"分裂、分隔\"，与 liberty/property 完全无关。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"conventions 表\"惯例、公约\"，比\"观念\"更偏制度化、不如 concepts 自然。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"excludes"},{"key":"B","text":"questions"},{"key":"C","text":"shapes"},{"key":"D","text":"controls"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"16.","reason":"上下文是\"法院处理社会政策决策\" When the court deals with social policy decisions, the law it __(16)__ is inescapably political——法院在处理社会政策时\"塑造的法律\"必然带有政治色彩。\"塑造\"对应 shapes。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"excludes 表\"排除\"，法院不是在排除法律，而是在解释和塑造法律。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"questions 表\"质疑\"，法院通常是裁断者而非质疑者。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"shapes 表\"塑造、形成\"，the law it shapes=\"它所塑造的法律\"，与\"法院判例塑造法律走向\"的事实严丝合缝。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"controls 表\"控制\"，过度强调权力关系，与\"塑造\"相比缺少\"通过判例形塑\"的精细含义。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"dismissed"},{"key":"B","text":"released"},{"key":"C","text":"ranked"},{"key":"D","text":"distorted"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"17.","reason":"as unjust 是补足语，决定动词性质 decisions split along ideological lines are so easily __(17)__ as unjust.——\"沿意识形态分裂的裁决很容易被……为不公正\"。be V-ed as unjust 即\"被斥为不公正\"，dismissed as 是地道的\"驳斥为\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"dismissed 与 as 构成 be dismissed as（被驳斥/否定为），\"轻易被斥为不公正\"承接\"沿意识形态分裂的裁决\"的负面后果完全自然。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"released 表\"被释放\"，be released as 无此用法。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"ranked 表\"排名\"，be ranked as 通常接等级，不接 unjust 这类道德评价。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"distorted 表\"扭曲\"，be distorted as 极少见，且语义\"被扭曲为不公正\"不通——裁决本身就被认为不公正，而不是被扭曲为不公正。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"suppress"},{"key":"B","text":"exploit"},{"key":"C","text":"address"},{"key":"D","text":"ignore"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"18.","reason":"下文 by making themselves accountable… 是方式状语，证明动作是\"消除疑虑\" The justices must __(18)__ doubts about the court's legitimacy by making themselves __(19)__ to the code of conduct. by 后给出的是建设性方式（接受守则），所以前面动作必是建设性的\"处理/消除\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"suppress 表\"压制\"，压制疑虑不是建设性回应。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"exploit 表\"利用\"，与正向方式矛盾。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"address 在此熟词僻义为\"处理、应对\"，address doubts 是地道搭配，且与 by 后的正向方式呼应。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"ignore 表\"忽视\"，与后文\"通过接受守则消除疑虑\"的方式句矛盾。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"accessible"},{"key":"B","text":"amiable"},{"key":"C","text":"agreeable"},{"key":"D","text":"accountable"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"19.","reason":"make themselves + ___ + to + the code of conduct making themselves __(19)__ 中的目标对象是\"守则\"，要的是\"对守则负责\"——be accountable to=\"对……负责\"是地道搭配。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"accessible 是\"可接近的\"，make oneself accessible to the public 还能讲通，但与\"行为守则\"搭配偏题。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"amiable 表\"和蔼可亲\"，描述人际态度，与守则无关。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"agreeable 表\"令人愉快、可同意的\"，与\"对守则负责\"不对应。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"accountable 与 to 构成 be accountable to（对……负责），make themselves accountable to the code of conduct=\"使自己对行为守则负责\"，与全文呼吁完全契合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"by all means"},{"key":"B","text":"at all costs"},{"key":"C","text":"in a word"},{"key":"D","text":"as a result"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"20.","reason":"前面\"看上去与政治分开\"→后面\"作为法律令人信服\"是因果 That would make rulings more likely to be seen as separate from politics and, __(20)__, convincing as law. 前后用 and 并列两个结果状语：\"裁决看上去与政治分开\"是直接结果，\"作为法律具有说服力\"是连带的进一步结果。本质是因果链。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"by all means 表\"无论如何、务必\"，是态度强调而非因果衔接。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"at all costs 表\"不惜一切代价\"，与本句因果链不搭。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"in a word 是\"一言以蔽之\"，用于多点总结后做结论；这里只有两个并列后果，且文章已近尾声但无多点总结，过强。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"as a result 表\"因此、结果\"，恰好连接\"被视为与政治分开\"与\"作为法律有说服力\"的因果——\"看上去独立，因此就更令人信服\"。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"Come on – Everybody's doing it. That whispered message, half invitation and half forcing, is what most of us think of when we hear the words peer pressure. It usually leads to no good—drinking, drugs and casual sex. But in her new book Join the Club, Tina Rosenberg contends that peer pressure can also be a positive force through what she calls the social cure, in which organizations and officials use the power of group dynamics to help individuals improve their lives and possibly the world."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"Rosenberg, the recipient of a Pulitzer Prize, offers a host of examples of the social cure in action: In South Carolina, a state-sponsored antismoking program called Rage Against the Haze sets out to make cigarettes uncool. In South Africa, an HIV-prevention initiative known as loveLife recruits young people to promote safe sex among their peers."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"The idea seems promising, and Rosenberg is a perceptive observer. Her critique of the lameness of many public-health campaigns is spot-on: they fail to mobilize peer pressure for healthy habits, and they demonstrate a seriously flawed understanding of psychology. \"Dare to be different, please don't smoke!\" pleads one billboard campaign aimed at reducing smoking among teenagers—teenagers, who desire nothing more than fitting in. Rosenberg argues convincingly that public-health advocates ought to take a page from advertisers, so skilled at applying peer pressure."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"But on the general effectiveness of the social cure, Rosenberg is less persuasive. Join the Club is filled with too much irrelevant detail and not enough exploration of the social and biological factors that make peer pressure so powerful. The most glaring flaw of the social cure as it's presented here is that it doesn't work very well for very long. Rage Against the Haze failed once state funding was cut. Evidence that the loveLife program produces lasting changes is limited and mixed."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"There's no doubt that our peer groups exert enormous influence on our behavior. An emerging body of research shows that positive health habits—as well as negative ones—spread through networks of friends via social communication. This is a subtle form of peer pressure: we unconsciously imitate the behavior we see every day."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-6","text":"Far less certain, however, is how successfully experts and bureaucrats can select our peer groups and steer their activities in virtuous directions. It's like the teacher who breaks up the troublemakers in the back row by pairing them with better-behaved classmates. The tactic never really works. And that's the problem with a social cure engineered from the outside: in the real world, as in school, we insist on choosing our own friends."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"According to the first paragraph, peer pressure often emerges as____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"a supplement to the social cure."},{"key":"B","text":"a stimulus to group dynamics."},{"key":"C","text":"an obstacle to social progress."},{"key":"D","text":"a cause of undesirable behaviors."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第一段,同伴压力往往表现为____","choicesZh":{"A":"社会治疗的补充","B":"群体动力的刺激因素","C":"社会进步的障碍","D":"不良行为的诱因"},"analysis":{"type":"According to the first paragraph, peer pressure often emerges as____ 明确指明段落、问客观事实，没有 infer/imply/suggest，是典型细节题。","parse":"According to the first paragraph, peer pressure often emerges as____ 是简单陈述句被改成填空：主干 peer pressure often emerges as ____，According to the first paragraph 是状语，emerges as = 表现为/呈现为，空格处填名词短语。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"It usually leads to no good—drinking, drugs and casual sex.","locateZh":"它（同辈压力）通常没什么好结果——酗酒、吸毒和随便发生性关系。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 peer pressure can also be a positive force through what she calls the social cure 显示 social cure 是 peer pressure 的一种应用，而非反过来 peer pressure 是 social cure 的补充。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"group dynamics 在原文是 Rosenberg 解释 social cure 的工具，并非「同辈压力通常表现为对它的刺激」。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说 peer pressure 通常导致酗酒、吸毒等个人不良行为，没说它阻碍「social progress（社会进步）」这种宏观概念。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"把「导致不良行为」对到四个选项，只有 a cause of undesirable behaviors. 与预判完全等值，直接锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"It usually leads to no good—drinking, drugs and casual sex","opt":"a cause of undesirable behaviors."}]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"Rosenberg holds that public-health advocates should____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"recruit professional advertisers."},{"key":"B","text":"learn from advertisers' experience."},{"key":"C","text":"stay away from commercial advertisers."},{"key":"D","text":"recognize the limitations of advertisements."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Rosenberg认为公共卫生倡导者应该____","choicesZh":{"A":"招募专业广告人员","B":"借鉴广告人员的经验","C":"远离商业广告人员","D":"认识到广告的局限性"},"analysis":{"type":"Rosenberg holds that public-health advocates should____ 问的是 Rosenberg 的具体建议，能在原文找到一句直接对应，属细节题。","parse":"Rosenberg holds that public-health advocates should____ 主干是 Rosenberg holds that …，that 后接宾语从句 public-health advocates should ____，空格处填动词原形短语。无陷阱。","locateEn":"Rosenberg argues convincingly that public-health advocates ought to take a page from advertisers, so skilled at applying peer pressure.","locateZh":"Rosenberg 颇有说服力地主张：公共卫生倡导者应当效仿广告人——后者非常擅长运用同辈压力。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 take a page from advertisers 只是「借鉴/学习」，不是 recruit professional advertisers.「招募广告人」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项里只有 learn from advertisers' experience. 与「借鉴广告人做法」语义等值，A/C/D 都偏离了 take a page from 的核心义。","pairs":[{"orig":"take a page from advertisers","opt":"learn from advertisers' experience."}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文是要「向广告人学习」，选项却说要 stay away from commercial advertisers.「远离商业广告人」，态度完全相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文没有让公共卫生倡导者去「认清广告局限性」；这一动作既不是 Rosenberg 的主张，也未出现在原句。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"In the author's view, Rosenberg's book fails to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"adequately probe social and biological factors."},{"key":"B","text":"effectively evade the flaws of the social cure."},{"key":"C","text":"illustrate the functions of state funding."},{"key":"D","text":"produce a long-lasting social effect."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在作者看来,Rosenberg的书未能____","choicesZh":{"A":"充分探究社会和生物因素","B":"有效规避社会治疗的缺陷","C":"阐明国家资助的功能","D":"产生持久的社会影响"},"analysis":{"type":"In the author's view, Rosenberg's book fails to____ 问的是作者已写出的具体批评，不是要考生推断，可在文中找到对应句，属细节题。","parse":"In the author's view, Rosenberg's book fails to____ 主干 Rosenberg's book fails to ____，In the author's view 是介词短语状语，fails to 后接动词原形。结构简单，但要警惕「作者 ≠ Rosenberg」这一立场归属。","locateEn":"Join the Club is filled with too much irrelevant detail and not enough exploration of the social and biological factors that make peer pressure so powerful.","locateZh":"《入会吧》一书塞满了过多无关细节，对让同辈压力如此强大的社会与生物学因素却探讨不足。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"题干本身已带否定 fails to，选项再正向描述「足够探究」 → 整体等值原文的「not enough exploration」，与预判完全对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"not enough exploration of the social and biological factors that make peer pressure so powerful","opt":"adequately probe social and biological factors."}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文从未要求该书去「绕开 social cure 的缺陷」，缺陷本身就是作者要书指出而 Rosenberg 没指出的对象，不是要去 evade 的对象。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 Rage Against the Haze failed once state funding was cut 只是用 state funding 解释项目失败的时机，从未要求书去「阐释州政府资助的功能」。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文是说 social cure 本身 doesn't work very well for very long，不是说「书产生不了持久社会效应」——长效与否的主语是项目，不是书。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"Paragraph 5 shows that our imitation of behaviors____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is harmful to our networks of friends."},{"key":"B","text":"will mislead behavioral studies."},{"key":"C","text":"occurs without our realizing it."},{"key":"D","text":"can produce negative health habits."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"第5段表明我们对行为的模仿____","choicesZh":{"A":"对我们的朋友网络有害","B":"会误导行为研究","C":"在我们未意识到的情况下发生","D":"可能产生不良健康习惯"},"analysis":{"type":"Paragraph 5 shows that our imitation of behaviors____ 问的是第 5 段呈现的客观事实，无 infer / imply，是细节题。","parse":"Paragraph 5 shows that our imitation of behaviors____ 主干 Paragraph 5 shows that …，that 后从句的主语是 our imitation of behaviors，空格填谓语动词短语。无陷阱。","locateEn":"This is a subtle form of peer pressure: we unconsciously imitate the behavior we see every day.","locateZh":"这是一种微妙的同辈压力：我们会在不知不觉中模仿每天看到的行为。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 spread through networks of friends 只说习惯通过朋友网络传播，没说模仿「伤害」朋友网络。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 An emerging body of research shows 是说研究表明同辈影响存在，不是说我们的模仿会 mislead behavioral studies. 把研究带偏。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"题干没有给方向词，只问「模仿……怎么样」；定位句最显眼的特征就是 unconsciously，能等值它的只有 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"we unconsciously imitate the behavior we see every day","opt":"occurs without our realizing it."}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 positive health habits—as well as negative ones 明确说正面与负面习惯都会被模仿传播；选项 can produce negative health habits. 只截取负面一半，丢掉了同等明示的正面部分。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"The author suggests in the last paragraph that the effect of peer pressure is____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"harmful."},{"key":"B","text":"desirable."},{"key":"C","text":"profound."},{"key":"D","text":"questionable."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者在最后一段暗示同伴压力的影响是____","choicesZh":{"A":"有害的","B":"可取的","C":"深远的","D":"值得质疑的"},"analysis":{"type":"The author suggests in the last paragraph that the effect of peer pressure is____ 选项 harmful. desirable. profound. questionable. 全是评价形容词，问的是作者对效果的判断极性，是典型态度题。","parse":"The author suggests in the last paragraph that the effect of peer pressure is____ 主干 The author suggests … that …，that 后从句主语 the effect of peer pressure，系动词 is 后填表语形容词。需特别注意 suggests 在此表示「暗示/含蓄表达」，不是「建议」。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"harmful. 是「有害」，但作者只质疑外部介入的有效性 never really works，并未指控 peer pressure 本身有害——本段甚至说自然产生的同辈影响是 subtle form，未否定。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"desirable. 是褒义「令人向往的」，与末段一连串怀疑/否定信号词完全相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"profound. 表「深远的、深刻的」，是中性偏褒，强调影响力之大；作者重点是「外部工程化是否有效」的怀疑，不是描述「影响力多深」。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"ABCD 四个评价形容词中，只有 questionable. 是怀疑极性，与作者末段一以贯之的怀疑口吻匹配，直接锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"Far less certain, however, is how successfully experts and bureaucrats can select our peer groups and steer their activities in virtuous directions","opt":"questionable."},{"orig":"The tactic never really works","opt":"questionable."}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"A deal is a deal—except, apparently, when Entergy is involved. The company, a major energy supplier in New England, provoked justified outrage in Vermont last week when it announced it was reneging on a longstanding commitment to abide by the state's strict nuclear regulations."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"Instead, the company has done precisely what it had long promised it would not: challenge the constitutionality of Vermont's rules in the federal court, as part of a desperate effort to keep its Vermont Yankee nuclear power plant running. It's a stunning move."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"The conflict has been surfacing since 2002, when the corporation bought Vermont's only nuclear power plant, an aging reactor in Vernon. As a condition of receiving state approval for the sale, the company agreed to seek permission from state regulators to operate past 2012. In 2006, the state went a step further, requiring that any extension of the plant's license be subject to the Vermont legislature's approval. Then, too, the company went along."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"Either Entergy never really intended to live by those commitments, or it simply didn't foresee what would happen next. A string of accidents, including the partial collapse of a cooling tower in 2007 and the discovery of an underground pipe system leakage, raised serious questions about both Vermont Yankee's safety and Entergy's management – especially after the company made misleading statements about the pipe. Enraged by Entergy's behavior, the Vermont Senate voted 26 to 4 last year against allowing an extension."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"Now the company is suddenly claiming that the 2002 agreement is invalid because of the 2006 legislation, and that only the federal government has regulatory power over nuclear issues. The legal issues in the case are obscure: whereas the Supreme Court has ruled that states do have some regulatory authority over nuclear power, legal scholars say that Vermont case will offer a precedent-setting test of how far those powers extend. Certainly, there are valid concerns about the patchwork regulations that could result if every state sets its own rules. But had Entergy kept its word, that debate would be beside the point."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-6","text":"The company seems to have concluded that its reputation in Vermont is already so damaged that it has nothing left to lose by going to war with the state. But there should be consequences. Permission to run a nuclear plant is a public trust. Entergy runs 11 other reactors in the United States, including Pilgrim Nuclear station in Plymouth. Pledging to run Pilgrim safely, the company has applied for federal permission to keep it open for another 20 years. But as the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) reviews the company's application, it should keep in mind what promises from Entergy are worth."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"The phrase \"reneging on\" (Line 3, Para. 1) is closest in meaning to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"condemning."},{"key":"B","text":"reaffirming."},{"key":"C","text":"dishonoring."},{"key":"D","text":"securing."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"短语\"reneging on\"(第一段第三行)在意思上最接近____","choicesZh":{"A":"谴责。","B":"重申。","C":"违背。","D":"获得。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The phrase \"reneging on\" (Line 3, Para. 1) is closest in meaning to 直接问某短语「意思最接近」，这是词义题的标志句式。","parse":"结构简单：主语 The phrase \"reneging on\" + 系动词短语 is closest in meaning to + 留空。无陷阱。","locateEn":"A deal is a deal—except, apparently, when Entergy is involved. The company, a major energy supplier in New England, provoked justified outrage in Vermont last week when it announced it was reneging on a longstanding commitment to abide by the state's strict nuclear regulations.","locateZh":"君子一言驷马难追——但 Entergy 显然不在其列。这家新英格兰主要能源供应商上周宣布将撕毁其长期承诺、不再遵守 Vermont 严苛的核监管规定，引发了该州正当的愤怒。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"condemning 意为「谴责」，主语应是 Vermont 才说得通；可句子主语是 Entergy 本身，逻辑反了。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"reaffirming 意为「再次确认、重申承诺」，与「Entergy 撕毁承诺、激起愤怒」的语境正相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的「违背承诺」类负面动词，四个选项里只有 dishonoring 同时具备负面极性与「对承诺/约定」搭配，与原文等值。","pairs":[{"orig":"reneging on a longstanding commitment to abide by the state's strict nuclear regulations","opt":"dishonoring"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"securing 意为「保住、确保」承诺被履行，与「撕约」相反；与下句 Instead, the company has done precisely what it had long promised it would not 完全冲突。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"By entering into the 2002 agreement, Entergy intended to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"obtain protection from Vermont regulators."},{"key":"B","text":"seek favor from the federal legislature."},{"key":"C","text":"acquire an extension of its business license."},{"key":"D","text":"get permission to purchase a power plant."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"通过签订2002年的协议,Entergy意图____","choicesZh":{"A":"获得Vermont监管机构的保护。","B":"寻求联邦立法机构的支持。","C":"获得其营业执照的延期。","D":"获得购买发电厂的许可。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 By entering into the 2002 agreement, Entergy intended to 问的是签 2002 协议「打算做什么」，是对原文一处客观事实的转述。","parse":"By entering into the 2002 agreement 是 by + 动名词作方式状语，等于「通过签 2002 协议（这一动作），公司想要……」，重点在主句 Entergy intended to 后的空格。","locateEn":"The conflict has been surfacing since 2002, when the corporation bought Vermont's only nuclear power plant, an aging reactor in Vernon. As a condition of receiving state approval for the sale, the company agreed to seek permission from state regulators to operate past 2012.","locateZh":"矛盾自 2002 年起就在浮现——那一年公司收购了 Vermont 唯一的核电站，即 Vernon 一座老化的反应堆。作为获得州方批准这笔收购的条件，公司同意（在 2012 年后继续运营时）须征得州监管机构许可。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"obtain protection from Vermont regulators 把 Vermont 监管者塑造成「保护者」，但原文里他们是 Entergy 须低头求许可的「监管者」，不是保护者。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"seek favor from the federal legislature 把对象从「state regulators / Vermont legislature」偷换成「federal legislature」；2002 协议是和州方谈的，与联邦无关。联邦法院只是第 2 段提到的 Entergy 后来撕约的去向。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"acquire an extension of its business license 是 Entergy 之后才追求的目标（2012 后想继续运营），而非 2002 签协议时的目的；2002 协议本身换的是「收购批准」，「延期」是它埋下的将来义务。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判要的是「换取收购批准」，get permission to purchase a power plant 把原文条件状语整段同义化，与预判逐字吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"As a condition of receiving state approval for the sale, the company agreed to seek permission from state regulators to operate past 2012","opt":"get permission to purchase a power plant"}]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"According to Paragraph 4, Entergy seems to have problems with its____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"managerial practices."},{"key":"B","text":"technical innovativeness."},{"key":"C","text":"financial goals."},{"key":"D","text":"business vision."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第四段,Entergy似乎在其____方面存在问题","choicesZh":{"A":"管理实践。","B":"技术创新性。","C":"财务目标。","D":"商业愿景。"},"analysis":{"type":"According to Paragraph 4 是细节题最经典开口，要求按段内事实回答。","parse":"主干 Entergy seems to have problems with its ____。seems 是软化语气，但不改变事实陈述性质；its 后接名词，提示选项都是名词性短语。","locateEn":"A string of accidents, including the partial collapse of a cooling tower in 2007 and the discovery of an underground pipe system leakage, raised serious questions about both Vermont Yankee's safety and Entergy's management – especially after the company made misleading statements about the pipe.","locateZh":"一连串事故——包括 2007 年冷却塔局部坍塌和地下管道系统泄漏的发现——引发了对 Vermont Yankee 安全性和 Entergy 管理水平的严重质疑，尤其是在公司就管道问题发表误导性声明之后。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"managerial practices 既同根替换了 Entergy's management，又承接了「误导性声明」这一具体做法，是预判的精准对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"Entergy's management","opt":"managerial practices"},{"orig":"made misleading statements about the pipe","opt":"managerial practices"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"technical innovativeness（技术创新性）在第 4 段毫无对应——事故描述的是「老旧 / 失修」，不是「创新与否」；段内没有任何关于创新的褒贬。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"financial goals（财务目标）在第 4 段无任何痕迹，段落只字未提钱、收益或预算。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"business vision（商业愿景）若说，也只能从第 6 段「申请 Pilgrim 延期 20 年」隐约延伸，但题干 According to Paragraph 4 已锁段，跨段证据不算。第 4 段本身只谈事故和管理。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"In the author's view, the Vermont case will test____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Entergy's capacity to fulfill all its promises."},{"key":"B","text":"the nature of states' patchwork regulations."},{"key":"C","text":"the federal authority over nuclear issues."},{"key":"D","text":"the limits of states' power over nuclear issues."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"在作者看来,Vermont案件将检验____","choicesZh":{"A":"Entergy履行其所有承诺的能力。","B":"各州拼凑式监管的性质。","C":"联邦在核问题上的权力。","D":"各州在核问题上的权力界限。"},"analysis":{"type":"In the author's view, the Vermont case will test ____ 实质要求转述原文那句「Vermont 案将测试什么」的论断，是有明确出处的细节题。","parse":"主干 the Vermont case will test ____，前置状语 In the author's view。空格处是 test 的宾语，选项均为名词性短语。","locateEn":"whereas the Supreme Court has ruled that states do have some regulatory authority over nuclear power, legal scholars say that Vermont case will offer a precedent-setting test of how far those powers extend.","locateZh":"尽管最高法院已裁定各州对核电确实拥有某些监管权，法律学者表示 Vermont 案将提供一次具有先例意义的检验，看这些权力究竟能延伸到多远。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Entergy's capacity to fulfill all its promises 是第 1、6 段的话题，本段法律焦点根本不在「Entergy 能不能守诺」上；况且 all 把范围放得过死。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the nature of states' patchwork regulations 把测试对象偷换成「拼布式监管的本质」；原文里 patchwork regulations 只是括号般的「担忧」，并非该案要测的内容。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"the federal authority over nuclear issues 把测试对象换成了「联邦的核监管权」；可定位句明确说测的是 states' powers，方向完全相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the limits of states' power over nuclear issues 同时承接「states' power（主体）」与「how far ... extend / limits（范围）」两层信息，与预判完全一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"how far those powers extend","opt":"the limits of states' power over nuclear issues"},{"orig":"states do have some regulatory authority over nuclear power","opt":"states' power over nuclear issues"}]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Entergy's business elsewhere might be affected."},{"key":"B","text":"the authority of the NRC will be defied."},{"key":"C","text":"Entergy will withdraw its Plymouth application."},{"key":"D","text":"Vermont's reputation might be damaged."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从最后一段可以推断出____","choicesZh":{"A":"Entergy在其他地方的业务可能会受到影响。","B":"NRC的权威将受到挑战。","C":"Entergy将撤回其Plymouth申请。","D":"Vermont的声誉可能会受损。"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that ____ 是推断题的模板句式。","parse":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that ____ 是 it 形式主语 + that 宾语从句，空格处填一个完整的陈述句。","locateEn":"Entergy runs 11 other reactors in the United States, including Pilgrim Nuclear station in Plymouth. Pledging to run Pilgrim safely, the company has applied for federal permission to keep it open for another 20 years. But as the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) reviews the company's application, it should keep in mind what promises from Entergy are worth.","locateZh":"Entergy 在美国还运营着 11 座反应堆，包括 Plymouth 的 Pilgrim 核电站。公司承诺会安全运营 Pilgrim，并已申请联邦许可让该站再开放 20 年。但 NRC 在审核这份申请时，应当掂量一下 Entergy 的承诺到底值几分。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Entergy's business elsewhere might be affected 把作者对 NRC 的暗示（应慎审）合规延伸为「Entergy 在别处的业务可能受影响」，且用 might 保留不确定性，恰与原文 should 的情态等量。","pairs":[{"orig":"as the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) reviews the company's application, it should keep in mind what promises from Entergy are worth","opt":"Entergy's business elsewhere might be affected"},{"orig":"Entergy runs 11 other reactors in the United States, including Pilgrim Nuclear station in Plymouth","opt":"Entergy's business elsewhere"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the authority of the NRC will be defied 说「NRC 的权威将被违抗」——原文恰恰是作者敦促 NRC 行使权威，谁也没说要违抗 NRC；且用 will 把可能性钉死。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Entergy will withdraw its Plymouth application 说 Entergy 自己将撤回 Pilgrim 申请——原文里申请人是 Entergy（仍在推进），而真正被作者寄望约束 Entergy 的是 NRC；让 Entergy「自撤」与全文「Entergy 撕约扩张」的姿态相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Vermont's reputation might be damaged 把 reputation 的所有者换成 Vermont；原文第 6 段开头 its reputation in Vermont is already so damaged 中的 its = Entergy's，受损的是 Entergy 在 Vermont 的声誉，不是 Vermont 自己的声誉。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"In the idealized version of how science is done, facts about the world are waiting to be observed and collected by objective researchers who use the scientific method to carry out their work. But in the everyday practice of science, discovery frequently follows an ambiguous and complicated route. We aim to be objective, but we cannot escape the context of our unique life experiences. Prior knowledge and interests influence what we experience, what we think our experiences mean, and the subsequent actions we take. Opportunities for misinterpretation, error, and self-deception abound."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"Consequently, discovery claims should be thought of as protoscience. Similar to newly staked mining claims, they are full of potential. But it takes collective scrutiny and acceptance to transform a discovery claim into a mature discovery. This is the credibility process, through which the individual researcher's me, here, now becomes the community's anyone, anywhere, anytime. Objective knowledge is the goal, not the starting point."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"Once a discovery claim becomes public, the discoverer receives intellectual credit. But, unlike with mining claims, the community takes control of what happens next. Within the complex social structure of the scientific community, researchers make discoveries; editors and reviewers act as gatekeepers by controlling the publication process; other scientists use the new finding to suit their own purposes; and finally, the public (including other scientists) receives the new discovery and possibly accompanying technology. As a discovery claim works its way through the community, the interaction and confrontation between shared and competing beliefs about the science and the technology involved transforms an individual's discovery claim into the community's credible discovery."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"Two paradoxes exist throughout this credibility process. First, scientific work tends to focus on some aspect of prevailing knowledge that is viewed as incomplete or incorrect. Little reward accompanies duplication and confirmation of what is already known and believed. The goal is new-search, not re-search. Not surprisingly, newly published discovery claims and credible discoveries that appear to be important and convincing will always be open to challenge and potential modification or refutation by future researchers. Second, novelty itself frequently provokes disbelief. Nobel Laureate and physiologist Albert Szent-Györgyi once described discovery as \"seeing what everybody has seen and thinking what nobody has thought.\" But thinking what nobody else has thought and telling others what they have missed may not change their views. Sometimes years are required for truly novel discovery claims to be accepted and appreciated."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"In the end, credibility \"happens\" to a discovery claim—a process that corresponds to what philosopher Annette Baier has described as the commons of the mind. \"We reason together, challenge, revise, and complete each other's reasoning and each other's conceptions of reason.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"According to the first paragraph, the process of discovery is characterized by its____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"uncertainty and complexity."},{"key":"B","text":"misconception and deceptiveness."},{"key":"C","text":"logicality and objectivity."},{"key":"D","text":"systematicness and regularity."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第一段,发现的过程具有怎样的特征","choicesZh":{"A":"不确定性和复杂性。","B":"误解性和欺骗性。","C":"逻辑性和客观性。","D":"系统性和规律性。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 According to the first paragraph 是 according to 型，且要求归纳 the process of discovery 的特征，属于段落级细节归纳。","parse":"主干是 the process of discovery is characterized by its____，过去分词短语作谓语，空格补的是介词 by 的宾语，应是名词性短语；its 提示该名词应是 discovery 本身的属性。","locateEn":"But in the everyday practice of science, discovery frequently follows an ambiguous and complicated route.","locateZh":"但在科学的日常实践中，发现往往沿着一条含糊而复杂的路径前行。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"uncertainty and complexity 同时覆盖了定位句的 ambiguous 与 complicated 两个核心修饰语，与预判完全吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"ambiguous","opt":"uncertainty"},{"orig":"complicated","opt":"complexity"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说存在 Opportunities for misinterpretation, error, and self-deception abound，即「机会很多」，并未把 misconception/deceptiveness 当作 discovery 过程本身的固有特征。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"logicality and objectivity 描述的是 the idealized version 那个被作者否定的版本，作者用 But 转折后明确指出现实并非如此。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"systematicness 与 regularity 描述的是有规律、成体系的过程，与定位句 ambiguous and complicated 直接矛盾。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 2 that credibility process requires____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"strict inspection."},{"key":"B","text":"shared efforts."},{"key":"C","text":"individual wisdom."},{"key":"D","text":"persistent innovation."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第二段可以推断出,可信度过程需要","choicesZh":{"A":"严格的检查。","B":"共同的努力。","C":"个人的智慧。","D":"持续的创新。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 It can be inferred from Paragraph 2 that credibility process requires____ 含 inferred，是典型推断题套式。","parse":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 2 that credibility process requires____ 是 It 作形式主语 + that 从句，重点在 that 后；空格做 requires 的宾语，应是名词性短语。","locateEn":"But it takes collective scrutiny and acceptance to transform a discovery claim into a mature discovery.","locateZh":"但要把一个发现性主张转化为成熟的发现，必须经过集体审视与接受。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"strict inspection 强调审视的「严苛程度」，原文只强调 collective 的「群体性」，未提强度，是把「集体的」偷换成「严格的」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"shared efforts 抽象覆盖了 collective scrutiny and acceptance 的「群体共同行动」核心义，与预判一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"collective scrutiny and acceptance","opt":"shared efforts"},{"orig":"the community's anyone, anywhere, anytime","opt":"shared"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"individual wisdom 强调个人智慧，而原文恰恰强调 the individual researcher's me, here, now becomes the community's anyone, anywhere, anytime，即要从「个人」走向「群体」，individual 与原文方向相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"persistent innovation 强调「持续创新」，第二段从未提及创新的持续性，是文中没有的概念。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"Paragraph 3 shows that a discovery claim becomes credible after it____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has attracted the attention of the general public."},{"key":"B","text":"has been examined by the scientific community."},{"key":"C","text":"has received recognition from editors and reviewers."},{"key":"D","text":"has been frequently quoted by peer scientists."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"第三段表明,一项发现声明在什么之后变得可信","choicesZh":{"A":"吸引了公众的注意。","B":"被科学界审查过。","C":"获得了编辑和审稿人的认可。","D":"被同行科学家频繁引用。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Paragraph 3 shows that a discovery claim becomes credible after it____ 是 X shows that 型，要求复述段内事实，属细节题。","parse":"Paragraph 3 shows that a discovery claim becomes credible after it____：主从结构，that 从句里 after 引导时间状语从句，空格是 after 从句的谓语成分，答案应是动作完成态。","locateEn":"As a discovery claim works its way through the community, the interaction and confrontation between shared and competing beliefs about the science and the technology involved transforms an individual's discovery claim into the community's credible discovery.","locateZh":"随着一个发现性主张在社群中流转，围绕相关科学与技术的共享信念与竞争信念之间的互动与交锋，把个人的发现性主张转化为社群层面的可信发现。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"the general public 指普通公众，而原文 the public (including other scientists) receives the new discovery 强调公众是「接收方」，且 credible 的转化机制是「社群」做的，不是「公众关注度」决定的。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"has been examined by the scientific community 把原文「在科学社群中经过互动与交锋」用「被科学社群审视」精准转述，且包含完成时态对应 after it ____ 的时态需要。","pairs":[{"orig":"works its way through the community","opt":"has been examined by the scientific community"},{"orig":"the interaction and confrontation between shared and competing beliefs","opt":"examined"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"editors and reviewers 只是原文 editors and reviewers act as gatekeepers 提到的若干角色之一，并非 credible 转化的全部主体，把其中一环当全过程。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"has been frequently quoted by peer scientists 涉及「被频繁引用」，原文从未提到引用次数或频率，是凭印象造出来的细节。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"Albert Szent-Györgyi would most likely agree that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"scientific claims will survive challenges."},{"key":"B","text":"discoveries today inspire future research."},{"key":"C","text":"efforts to make discoveries are justified."},{"key":"D","text":"scientific work calls for a critical mind."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"Albert Szent-Györgyi最可能同意","choicesZh":{"A":"科学声明将经受住挑战。","B":"今天的发现启发未来的研究。","C":"做出发现的努力是正当的。","D":"科学工作需要批判性思维。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 would most likely agree 是经典「人物观点引申」型，要求从此人原话推一步。","parse":"Albert Szent-Györgyi would most likely agree that____：主语是人名，would agree that 引导宾语从句，空格内填一个完整命题（主谓齐全的从句）。","locateEn":"Nobel Laureate and physiologist Albert Szent-Györgyi once described discovery as \"seeing what everybody has seen and thinking what nobody has thought.\" But thinking what nobody else has thought and telling others what they have missed may not change their views.","locateZh":"诺贝尔奖得主、生理学家阿尔伯特·圣捷尔吉曾把发现描述为「看人人所见，想无人所想」。但是，想出别人没想过的、并把别人所漏看的告诉他们，未必能改变他们的看法。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"scientific claims will survive challenges 的观点来自 newly published discovery claims and credible discoveries ... will always be open to challenge 这一作者本人的陈述，而非 Szent-Györgyi 的引文。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"discoveries today inspire future research 强调「今日发现激发未来研究」，是常识但非 Szent-Györgyi 引文所谈，引文只论「看见与思考」，不论代际激发。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"efforts to make discoveries are justified 谈「为做出发现而付出努力是有道理的」，与 Szent-Györgyi 引文的「思维方式」无关，文不对题。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"scientific work calls for a critical mind 与预判「独立批判思考」高度一致，是 Szent-Györgyi 引文最自然的一步引申。","pairs":[{"orig":"thinking what nobody has thought","opt":"a critical mind"},{"orig":"seeing what everybody has seen and thinking what nobody has thought","opt":"scientific work calls for"}]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title of the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Novelty as an Engine of Scientific Development."},{"key":"B","text":"Collective Scrutiny in Scientific Discovery."},{"key":"C","text":"Evolution of Credibility in Doing Science."},{"key":"D","text":"Challenge to Credibility at the Gate to Science."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"以下哪项最适合作为本文的标题?","choicesZh":{"A":"新颖性作为科学发展的引擎。","B":"科学发现中的集体审查。","C":"科学研究中可信度的演变。","D":"科学门槛上对可信度的挑战。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Which of the following would be the best title of the text? 要求选最佳标题，主旨题无疑。","parse":"Which of the following would be the best title of the text? 是 which 引导的特殊疑问句，主干结构清晰，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Novelty as an Engine of Scientific Development 只覆盖 P4 关于 novelty 的局部讨论，第一、二、三、五段几乎都不谈 novelty 作为「引擎」，主题被缩窄。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Collective Scrutiny in Scientific Discovery 只对应 collective scrutiny and acceptance 这一环节，未涵盖 P4 的悖论与 P5 的 commons of the mind 等收束内容。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Evolution of Credibility in Doing Science 同时包含核心对象（Credibility）、动态属性（Evolution）与场景（Doing Science），与预判完全对位，且能覆盖全部五段。","pairs":[{"orig":"credibility process","opt":"Credibility"},{"orig":"In the end, credibility \"happens\" to a discovery claim","opt":"Evolution of Credibility"},{"orig":"As a discovery claim works its way through the community","opt":"in Doing Science"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Challenge to Credibility at the Gate to Science 把 editors and reviewers act as gatekeepers 拆出来当全文主题，且把整体「可信性的形成过程」偷换为「对可信性的挑战」，焦点全错。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"If the trade unionist Jimmy Hoffa were alive today, he would probably represent civil servants. When Hoffa's Teamsters were in their prime in 1960, only one in ten American government workers belonged to a union; now 36% do. In 2009 the number of unionists in America's public sector passed that of their fellow members in the private sector. In Britain, more than half of public-sector workers but only about 15% of private-sector ones are unionized."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"There are three reasons for the public-sector unions' thriving. First, they can shut things down without suffering much in the way of consequences. Second, they are mostly bright and well-educated. A quarter of America's public-sector workers have a university degree. Third, they now dominate left-of-centre politics. Some of their ties go back a long way. Britain's Labor Party, as its name implies, has long been associated with trade unionism. Its current leader, Ed Miliband, owes his position to votes from public-sector unions."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"At the state level their influence can be even more fearsome. Mark Baldassare of the Public Policy Institute of California points out that much of the state's budget is patrolled by unions. The teachers' unions keep an eye on schools, the CCPOA on prisons and a variety of labor groups on health care."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"In many rich countries average wages in the state sector are higher than in the private one. But the real gains come in benefits and work practices. Politicians have repeatedly \"backloaded\" public-sector pay deals, keeping the pay increases modest but adding to holidays and especially pensions that are already generous."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"Reform has been vigorously opposed, perhaps most notoriously in education, where charter schools, academies and merit pay all faced drawn-out battles. Even though there is plenty of evidence that the quality of the teachers is the most important variable, teachers' unions have fought against getting rid of bad ones and promoting good ones."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"As the cost to everyone else has become clearer, politicians have begun to clamp down. In Wisconsin the unions have rallied thousands of supporters against Scott Walker, the hardline Republican governor. But many within the public sector suffer under the current system, too."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-7","text":"John Donahue at Harvard's Kennedy School points out that the norms of culture in Western civil services suit those who want to stay put but are bad for high achievers. The only American public-sector workers who earn well above $250,000 a year are university sports coaches and the president of the United States. Bankers' fat pay packets have attracted much criticism, but a public-sector system that does not reward high achievers may be a much bigger problem for America."}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"It can be learned from the first paragraph that____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Teamsters still have a large body of members."},{"key":"B","text":"Jimmy Hoffa used to work as a civil servant."},{"key":"C","text":"unions have enlarged their public-sector membership."},{"key":"D","text":"the government has improved its relationship with unionists."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从第一段可以得知____","choicesZh":{"A":"Teamsters 仍然拥有大量成员。","B":"Jimmy Hoffa 曾经担任公务员。","C":"工会扩大了其公共部门的成员数量。","D":"政府改善了与工会成员的关系。"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be learned from the first paragraph that 是中性的「可以得知」句式，没有 infer/imply/suggest 等推断词，问的是段内可被直接读出的事实。","parse":"It can be learned from the first paragraph that____ 是「形式主语 it + 被动 can be learned + from 状语 + that 引导宾语从句空位」的标准残句句式，that 之后留空给选项续写；考生只需把每个选项代入 that 之后通读一遍即可，无陷阱。","locateEn":"When Hoffa's Teamsters were in their prime in 1960, only one in ten American government workers belonged to a union; now 36% do. In 2009 the number of unionists in America's public sector passed that of their fellow members in the private sector.","locateZh":"当 Hoffa 的卡车司机工会 1960 年处于鼎盛时，每十个美国政府工人中只有一个加入工会；如今则有 36%。2009 年，美国公共部门工会会员人数超过了私人部门会员人数。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 Hoffa's Teamsters were in their prime in 1960 明示卡车司机工会的鼎盛是 1960 年的事，且全段未提到该工会今日的规模；A 项 Teamsters still have a large body of members 中的 still 把过去式偷换成现在仍然，原文无据。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 If the trade unionist Jimmy Hoffa were alive today, he would probably represent civil servants 是非真实条件句，意思是「若他今天还活着，他大概会代表公务员」——是一个假设性预测；B 项 Jimmy Hoffa used to work as a civil servant 把它转写为「他过去当过公务员」的历史事实，与假设语气完全不符。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项 unions have enlarged their public-sector membership 同时覆盖了「36% 入会率」与「公共部门超过私人部门」两条数据所共同指向的「工会在公共部门扩张」这一结论，正中预判。","pairs":[{"orig":"only one in ten American government workers belonged to a union; now 36% do","opt":"unions have enlarged their public-sector membership"},{"orig":"the number of unionists in America's public sector passed that of their fellow members in the private sector","opt":"their public-sector membership"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"P1 全段只罗列入会率数据，未涉及政府与工会的关系如何（紧张/缓和/改善/恶化）；D 项 the government has improved its relationship with unionists 整句无原文支撑。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"Which of the following is true of Paragraph 2?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Public-sector unions are prudent in taking actions."},{"key":"B","text":"Education is required for public-sector union membership."},{"key":"C","text":"Labor Party has long been fighting against public-sector unions."},{"key":"D","text":"Public-sector unions seldom get in trouble for their actions."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"关于第二段,下列哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"公共部门工会在采取行动时是谨慎的。","B":"公共部门工会成员资格需要教育背景。","C":"工党长期以来一直在与公共部门工会作斗争。","D":"公共部门工会很少因其行动而陷入困境。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true of Paragraph 2 用 which...is true 句式，要求把四个选项与第二段事实逐一核对，是典型的「四选一真伪」细节题。","parse":"Which of the following is true of Paragraph 2? 由疑问代词 which 作主语、of the following 作后置定语、is true of Paragraph 2 作系表结构构成，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"First, they can shut things down without suffering much in the way of consequences.","locateZh":"第一，他们可以让事情停摆，而自己几乎不会因此承担什么后果。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 they can shut things down without suffering much in the way of consequences 表明工会有恃无恐、敢于关停服务；A 项 Public-sector unions are prudent in taking actions 说他们行事审慎，与原文「敢于关停且不担后果」的语气完全相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 A quarter of America's public-sector workers have a university degree 只是一个 25% 的统计事实，不是入会门槛；B 项 Education is required for public-sector union membership 把统计事实曲解成入会硬性条件。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 Britain's Labor Party, as its name implies, has long been associated with trade unionism 表明工党与工会主义长期绑定（associated with），是支持关系；C 项 Labor Party has long been fighting against public-sector unions 把「绑定/支持」反转为「对抗」，方向完全颠倒。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 项 Public-sector unions seldom get in trouble for their actions 把第一条理由整句重写：seldom 对应 without...much、get in trouble for their actions 对应 suffering...consequences (when they shut things down)，正中预判。","pairs":[{"orig":"without suffering much in the way of consequences","opt":"seldom get in trouble for their actions"},{"orig":"they can shut things down","opt":"for their actions"}]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"It can be learned from Paragraph 4 that the income in the state sector is____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"illegally secured."},{"key":"B","text":"indirectly augmented."},{"key":"C","text":"excessively increased."},{"key":"D","text":"fairly adjusted."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第四段可以得知,国有部门的收入是____","choicesZh":{"A":"非法获得的。","B":"间接增加的。","C":"过度增长的。","D":"公平调整的。"},"analysis":{"type":"the income in the state sector is____ 是结论残句，需要从 P4 中关于「明面工资温和涨、福利与养老金大涨」的事实推出一步结论：收入是被「以另一种方式」做大的。","parse":"It can be learned from Paragraph 4 that the income in the state sector is____ 主干是 it can be learned that... 的形式主语句，that 从句的真实主语是 the income in the state sector，is 之后留待选项补充表语，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"But the real gains come in benefits and work practices. Politicians have repeatedly \"backloaded\" public-sector pay deals, keeping the pay increases modest but adding to holidays and especially pensions that are already generous.","locateZh":"但真正的好处出现在福利与工作待遇上。政界一再「后置加码」公共部门的薪资协议——把薪资涨幅压得温和，却追加假期、尤其追加本已优厚的养老金。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说政界「重复地把薪资协议后置加码」，Politicians have repeatedly \"backloaded\" public-sector pay deals 是描述操作手法，未做任何合法性判断；A 项 illegally secured 把「不透明」直接升格为「违法」，远超原文。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 项 indirectly augmented 同时捕捉了「明面温和（不直接加）」与「暗面加码（实质增加）」两层语义，是对 backloaded 机制最精准的一步推断。","pairs":[{"orig":"keeping the pay increases modest but adding to holidays and especially pensions","opt":"indirectly augmented"},{"orig":"Politicians have repeatedly \"backloaded\" public-sector pay deals","opt":"indirectly augmented"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 keeping the pay increases modest 明示薪资涨幅是「温和的」，仅福利/养老金部分被加码，整体远谈不上「过度」；C 项 excessively increased 用 excessively（过度地）把温和涨幅夸大为过度增长，是程度偷改。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文未提任何「fair/公正」「adjusted/经过适当调整」的评价信息——backloaded 一词的暗讽倾向恰恰相反；D 项 fairly adjusted 凭空加入褒义评价。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"The example of the unions in Wisconsin shows that unions____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"often run against the current political system."},{"key":"B","text":"can change people's political attitudes."},{"key":"C","text":"may be a barrier to public-sector reforms."},{"key":"D","text":"are dominant in the government."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"Wisconsin 工会的例子表明工会____","choicesZh":{"A":"经常与当前政治体制相对抗。","B":"能够改变人们的政治态度。","C":"可能成为公共部门改革的障碍。","D":"在政府中占据主导地位。"},"analysis":{"type":"The example of the unions in Wisconsin shows that unions____ 中 shows that 直接点明问例证之目的，是教科书式的例证目的题题干。","parse":"The example of the unions in Wisconsin shows that unions____ 主语是 the example...in Wisconsin（the example 后接两层 of/in 介词短语作后置定语），谓语 shows 带 that 宾语从句，从句主语是 unions、谓语留空待选项补出。考生只要把 the example...shows that 看成「举该例是为了说明...」即可。","locateEn":"As the cost to everyone else has become clearer, politicians have begun to clamp down. In Wisconsin the unions have rallied thousands of supporters against Scott Walker, the hardline Republican governor.","locateZh":"随着工会带给其他所有人的代价日益清晰，政客们已开始出手压制。在威斯康星州，工会动员了数千名支持者抗议强硬派共和党州长 Scott Walker。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 the unions have rallied thousands of supporters against Scott Walker, the hardline Republican governor 对抗的是某位州长本人推动的改革，而非「现行政治体制」；A 项 often run against the current political system 把具体对抗对象升格为「整个政治体制」，是范围偏移；且 often 暗示常态化，原文只举一例，不足支撑。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说工会「动员了数千名既有支持者」抗议州长（rallied thousands of supporters），并未说工会改变了任何人的政治态度；B 项 can change people's political attitudes 把「动员既有支持者」过度推断为「改变政治态度」。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项 may be a barrier to public-sector reforms 用情态 may 与名词 barrier 准确捕捉了「工会构成改革阻力」这一论点；其他选项要么偷换主体、要么偷换议题，唯有 C 命中例证所要证明的论点。","pairs":[{"orig":"Reform has been vigorously opposed","opt":"may be a barrier to public-sector reforms"},{"orig":"the unions have rallied thousands of supporters against Scott Walker, the hardline Republican governor","opt":"public-sector reforms"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文描述的是工会「对抗」州长，即处于反对方位置；并未表明工会主导政府运作。D 项 are dominant in the government 与「与政府方对抗」的语境完全相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"John Donahue's attitude towards the public-sector system is one of____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"disapproval."},{"key":"B","text":"appreciation."},{"key":"C","text":"tolerance."},{"key":"D","text":"indifference."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"态度题","stemZh":"John Donahue 对公共部门体制的态度是____","choicesZh":{"A":"不赞成。","B":"赞赏。","C":"容忍。","D":"漠不关心。"},"analysis":{"type":"John Donahue's attitude towards the public-sector system is one of____ 用 attitude towards 直接锁定为态度题，问 Donahue 对 the public-sector system 的褒贬态度。","parse":"John Donahue's attitude towards the public-sector system is one of____ 主语是 John Donahue's attitude（attitude 由 towards 短语作后置定语），系动词 is，表语 one of ____ 留空给选项补出态度名词；one of 后接抽象名词是态度题最常见的留空形式，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"A 项 disapproval 是四选项中唯一明确的负面态度词，B/C/D 分别为褒义/容忍/漠不关心，与段内 bad、bigger problem 的负面极性精确匹配。","pairs":[{"orig":"are bad for high achievers","opt":"disapproval"},{"orig":"a public-sector system that does not reward high achievers may be a much bigger problem for America","opt":"disapproval"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Donahue 在 P7 全段对公共部门体系无一句肯定，没有 good/admirable/effective 等褒义评价；B 项 appreciation 与段内 bad、bigger problem 的负面定性完全相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"tolerance（容忍）暗含「虽不满但能接受」的态度，而 Donahue 用 a much bigger problem 直接定性为更严重的问题，a public-sector system that does not reward high achievers may be a much bigger problem for America 显示他在主动呼吁警惕，而非「勉强接受」。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Donahue 在 may be a much bigger problem for America 中用 much bigger problem for America 强调问题的严重性与影响范围，明显投入了立场而非冷淡观望；D 项 indifference 与他段内集中输出评价的姿态相反。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"matching","title":"Section II Part B 选句填空","directions":"Directions: In the following text, some sentences have been removed. For Questions 41 – 45, choose the most suitable one from the list A – G to fit into each of the numbered blanks. There are two extra choices, which do not fit in any of the blanks. Mark your answers on ANSWER SHEET 1. (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"","text":"Think of those fleeting moments when you look out of an aeroplane window and realise that you are flying, higher than a bird. Now think of your laptop, thinner than a brown-paper envelope, or your cellphone in the palm of your hand. Take a moment or two to wonder at those marvels. You are the lucky inheritor of a dream come true."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"","text":"The second half of the 20th century saw a collection of geniuses, warriors, entrepreneurs and visionaries labour to create a fabulous machine that could function as a typewriter and printing press, studio and theatre, paintbrush and gallery, piano and radio, the mail as well as the mail carrier. {{41}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"","text":"The networked computer is an amazing device, the first media machine that serves as the mode of production, means of distribution, site of reception, and place of praise and critique. The computer is the 21st century's culture machine."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"","text":"But for all the reasons there are to celebrate the computer, we must also act with caution. {{42}} I call it a secret war for two reasons. First, most people do not realise that there are strong commercial agendas at work to keep them in passive consumption mode. Second, the majority of people who use networked computers to upload are not even aware of the significance of what they are doing."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"","text":"All animals download, but only a few upload. Beavers build dams and birds make nests. Yet for the most part, the animal kingdom moves through the world downloading. Humans are unique in their capacity to not only make tools but then turn around and use them to create superfluous material goods – paintings, sculpture and architecture – and superfluous experiences – music, literature, religion and philosophy. {{43}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"","text":"For all the possibilities of our new culture machines, most people are still stuck in download mode. Even after the advent of widespread social media, a pyramid of production remains, with a small number of people uploading material, a slightly larger group commenting on or modifying that content, and a huge percentage remaining content to just consume. {{44}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-7","label":"","text":"Television is a one-way tap flowing into our homes. The hardest task that television asks of anyone is to turn the power off after he has turned it on. {{45}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-8","label":"","text":"What counts as meaningful uploading? My definition revolves around the concept of \"stickiness\" – creations and experiences to which others adhere."}]},"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Of course, it is precisely these superfluous things that define human culture and ultimately what it is to be human. Downloading and consuming culture requires great skills, but failing to move beyond downloading is to strip oneself of a defining constituent of humanity."},{"key":"B","text":"Applications like tumblr.com, which allow users to combine pictures, words and other media in creative ways and then share them, have the potential to add stickiness by amusing, entertaining and enlightening others."},{"key":"C","text":"Not only did they develop such a device, but by the turn of the millennium they had also managed to embed it in a worldwide system accessed by billions of people every day."},{"key":"D","text":"This is because the networked computer has sparked a secret war between downloading and uploading – between passive consumption and active creation – whose outcome will shape our collective future in ways we can only begin to imagine."},{"key":"E","text":"The challenge the computer mounts to television thus bears little similarity to one format being replaced by another in the manner of record players being replaced by CD players."},{"key":"F","text":"One reason for the persistence of this pyramid of production is that for the past half-century, much of the world's media culture has been defined by a single medium – television – and television is defined by downloading."},{"key":"G","text":"The networked computer offers the first chance in 50 years to reverse the flow, to encourage thoughtful downloading and, even more importantly, meaningful uploading."}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Of course, it is precisely these superfluous things that define human culture and ultimately what it is to be human. Downloading and consuming culture requires great skills, but failing to move beyond downloading is to strip oneself of a defining constituent of humanity."},{"key":"B","text":"Applications like tumblr.com, which allow users to combine pictures, words and other media in creative ways and then share them, have the potential to add stickiness by amusing, entertaining and enlightening others."},{"key":"C","text":"Not only did they develop such a device, but by the turn of the millennium they had also managed to embed it in a worldwide system accessed by billions of people every day."},{"key":"D","text":"This is because the networked computer has sparked a secret war between downloading and uploading – between passive consumption and active creation – whose outcome will shape our collective future in ways we can only begin to imagine."},{"key":"E","text":"The challenge the computer mounts to television thus bears little similarity to one format being replaced by another in the manner of record players being replaced by CD players."},{"key":"F","text":"One reason for the persistence of this pyramid of production is that for the past half-century, much of the world's media culture has been defined by a single medium – television – and television is defined by downloading."},{"key":"G","text":"The networked computer offers the first chance in 50 years to reverse the flow, to encourage thoughtful downloading and, even more importantly, meaningful uploading."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"段末","stemZh":"41. (41)____","reason":"Not only did they develop such a device, but by the turn of the millennium they had also managed to embed it in a worldwide system accessed by billions of people every day. 他们不仅开发出了这样一种设备,而且到千禧年之交,他们还成功地将其嵌入到一个每天有数十亿人访问的全球系统中。\n承接\"造出一台全能机器\"，补一句进一步成就 空前一句是第 2 段主体：The second half of the 20th century saw a collection of geniuses, warriors, entrepreneurs and visionaries labour to create a fabulous machine，讲一群人\"造出了一台神奇机器\"；空 41 独占段末。下一段第 3 段开头 The networked computer is an amazing device 已跳到\"联网计算机\"。所以这个空要补一句\"他们不仅造出机器、还进一步把它怎样了\"的递进句，自然过渡到\"联网\"这一层。\nNot only 递进+they/such a device 回指+引出全球系统，三钩全中 C 逐条对上：① Not only did they develop such a device, but … they had also managed 的\"不仅…而且…\"正是所需递进；② they 接上文那群人、such a device 接 a fabulous machine，代词全有着落；③ embed it in a worldwide system accessed by billions of people every day 正好为下段 The networked computer 的\"networked\"铺路。上接\"造出机器\"、下引\"联网计算机\"，双向缝合。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Not only did they develop such a device, but by the turn of the millennium they had also managed to embed it in a worldwide system accessed by billions of people every day.","clues":["代词指代 正确句须有 they/such a device 回指上文 空前句的主语是 a collection of geniuses, warriors, entrepreneurs and visionaries(一群人)、宾语是 a fabulous machine(一台机器)。要补的句子若用代词承接，理应用\"他们\"指这群人、用\"这样一台设备\"指这台机器——正确句应自带这两个回指词。","逻辑连接 须为递进逻辑，并引出\"联网/全球系统\" 空后是段落边界，下段开头是 The networked computer is an amazing device，凭空冒出\"networked(联网)\"。故正确句须在\"造出机器\"之上再递进一层、并把机器接入某种\"全球/联网系统\"，为下段的\"networked computer\"铺路——即一个\"不仅…而且…\"的递进结构。"]}},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Of course, it is precisely these superfluous things that define human culture and ultimately what it is to be human. Downloading and consuming culture requires great skills, but failing to move beyond downloading is to strip oneself of a defining constituent of humanity."},{"key":"B","text":"Applications like tumblr.com, which allow users to combine pictures, words and other media in creative ways and then share them, have the potential to add stickiness by amusing, entertaining and enlightening others."},{"key":"C","text":"Not only did they develop such a device, but by the turn of the millennium they had also managed to embed it in a worldwide system accessed by billions of people every day."},{"key":"D","text":"This is because the networked computer has sparked a secret war between downloading and uploading – between passive consumption and active creation – whose outcome will shape our collective future in ways we can only begin to imagine."},{"key":"E","text":"The challenge the computer mounts to television thus bears little similarity to one format being replaced by another in the manner of record players being replaced by CD players."},{"key":"F","text":"One reason for the persistence of this pyramid of production is that for the past half-century, much of the world's media culture has been defined by a single medium – television – and television is defined by downloading."},{"key":"G","text":"The networked computer offers the first chance in 50 years to reverse the flow, to encourage thoughtful downloading and, even more importantly, meaningful uploading."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"段中","stemZh":"42. (42)____","reason":"This is because the networked computer has sparked a secret war between downloading and uploading – between passive consumption and active creation – whose outcome will shape our collective future in ways we can only begin to imagine. 这是因为联网计算机引发了一场下载与上传之间、被动消费与主动创造之间的秘密战争,其结果将以我们只能初步想象的方式塑造我们的集体未来。\n为\"须谨慎\"给出原因，并引出\"隐秘之战\"供下文解释 空前句是 But for all the reasons there are to celebrate the computer, we must also act with caution.——抛出一个判断\"也须谨慎\"，但没说为什么。空后紧跟 I call it a secret war for two reasons.——直接说\"我把它叫作一场隐秘之战\"。前有待解释的结论、后有 it 与 secret war 凭空出现，所以这个空必须补一句\"之所以须谨慎，是因为……一场 secret war\"，承前因、启后文。\nThis is because 承前因+首次引出 secret war 供下句复现 D 全中：① This is because 正是\"须谨慎\"所需的因果承接；② has sparked a secret war between downloading and uploading 第一次正式抛出 secret war，下句 I call it a secret war for two reasons. 的 it 与 secret war 由此获得先行词，词汇复现严丝合缝；③ 它把全文主命题(下载 vs 上传之战)正式点出，与全局脉络高度自洽。","options":{},"choiceEn":"This is because the networked computer has sparked a secret war between downloading and uploading – between passive consumption and active creation – whose outcome will shape our collective future in ways we can only begin to imagine.","clues":["逻辑连接 须给出\"须谨慎\"的原因 空前 we must also act with caution. 是一个未解释的结论，正确句须以\"这是因为……\"的因果逻辑承接，给出\"为何要谨慎\"。","词汇复现 正确句须首次引出 secret war 供下句复现 空后句 I call it a secret war for two reasons. 里的 it 和 secret war 都是\"已知信息\"的口吻，说明这个词在空里已经第一次出现过。正确句必须自带 secret war 这一短语(或其全称)，下句才能用 it/a secret war 复现。"]}},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Of course, it is precisely these superfluous things that define human culture and ultimately what it is to be human. Downloading and consuming culture requires great skills, but failing to move beyond downloading is to strip oneself of a defining constituent of humanity."},{"key":"B","text":"Applications like tumblr.com, which allow users to combine pictures, words and other media in creative ways and then share them, have the potential to add stickiness by amusing, entertaining and enlightening others."},{"key":"C","text":"Not only did they develop such a device, but by the turn of the millennium they had also managed to embed it in a worldwide system accessed by billions of people every day."},{"key":"D","text":"This is because the networked computer has sparked a secret war between downloading and uploading – between passive consumption and active creation – whose outcome will shape our collective future in ways we can only begin to imagine."},{"key":"E","text":"The challenge the computer mounts to television thus bears little similarity to one format being replaced by another in the manner of record players being replaced by CD players."},{"key":"F","text":"One reason for the persistence of this pyramid of production is that for the past half-century, much of the world's media culture has been defined by a single medium – television – and television is defined by downloading."},{"key":"G","text":"The networked computer offers the first chance in 50 years to reverse the flow, to encourage thoughtful downloading and, even more importantly, meaningful uploading."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"段末","stemZh":"43. (43)____","reason":"Of course, it is precisely these superfluous things that define human culture and ultimately what it is to be human. Downloading and consuming culture requires great skills, but failing to move beyond downloading is to strip oneself of a defining constituent of humanity. 当然,正是这些多余的东西定义了人类文化,并最终定义了作为人类的本质。下载和消费文化需要高超的技能,但如果不能超越下载,就是在剥夺自己人性的一个决定性组成部分。\n为\"人类制造多余之物\"作总结升华 空前句是第 5 段的论点核心：Humans are unique in their capacity to not only make tools but then turn around and use them to create superfluous material goods … and superfluous experiences …——人类独特之处在于创造各种\"多余\"(superfluous)之物与体验。空 43 独占段末，且第 6 段另起话题(download mode)。所以这个空要补一句对本段\"superfluous\"论点的总结升华：正是这些多余之物定义了人性。\nOf course 顺接+复现 superfluous+升华到\"人性\"，总结到位 A 全中：① Of course, it is precisely these superfluous things 用 Of course 顺接、these superfluous things 直接回指上文两个 superfluous；② that define human culture and ultimately what it is to be human 把多余之物升华为\"何以为人\"，是教科书式的段末总结；③ failing to move beyond downloading is to strip oneself of a defining constituent of humanity 又把话题引向 downloading，恰好衔接第 6 段的 download mode。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Of course, it is precisely these superfluous things that define human culture and ultimately what it is to be human. Downloading and consuming culture requires great skills, but failing to move beyond downloading is to strip oneself of a defining constituent of humanity.","clues":["词汇复现 正确句须复现 superfluous 空前句把 superfluous material goods 与 superfluous experiences 连说两遍，superfluous 是本段题眼。作为段末总结句，正确句极可能再次出现 superfluous，把它从\"多余之物\"升华到\"人性\"层面。","结构功能 段末须补总结/升华句 由 43 独占段末、且第 6 段 most people are still stuck in download mode. 另起新话题可知，本空承担\"对第 5 段做收束总结\"的结构功能，应是一句对前述论点的拔高定论，而非引出新例。"]}},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Of course, it is precisely these superfluous things that define human culture and ultimately what it is to be human. Downloading and consuming culture requires great skills, but failing to move beyond downloading is to strip oneself of a defining constituent of humanity."},{"key":"B","text":"Applications like tumblr.com, which allow users to combine pictures, words and other media in creative ways and then share them, have the potential to add stickiness by amusing, entertaining and enlightening others."},{"key":"C","text":"Not only did they develop such a device, but by the turn of the millennium they had also managed to embed it in a worldwide system accessed by billions of people every day."},{"key":"D","text":"This is because the networked computer has sparked a secret war between downloading and uploading – between passive consumption and active creation – whose outcome will shape our collective future in ways we can only begin to imagine."},{"key":"E","text":"The challenge the computer mounts to television thus bears little similarity to one format being replaced by another in the manner of record players being replaced by CD players."},{"key":"F","text":"One reason for the persistence of this pyramid of production is that for the past half-century, much of the world's media culture has been defined by a single medium – television – and television is defined by downloading."},{"key":"G","text":"The networked computer offers the first chance in 50 years to reverse the flow, to encourage thoughtful downloading and, even more importantly, meaningful uploading."}],"answer":"F","explanation":{"answer":"F","type":"段末","stemZh":"44. (44)____","reason":"One reason for the persistence of this pyramid of production is that for the past half-century, much of the world's media culture has been defined by a single medium – television – and television is defined by downloading. 这种生产金字塔持续存在的一个原因是,在过去半个世纪里,世界上大部分媒体文化都是由单一媒介——电视——所定义的,而电视的特点就是下载。\n为\"生产金字塔仍在\"补一条原因，并引出电视 空前句是第 6 段核心：a pyramid of production remains, with a small number of people uploading material … and a huge percentage remaining content to just consume.——指出\"生产金字塔\"依然存在。空 44 独占段末，第 7 段开头突然变成 Television is a one-way tap flowing into our homes.——凭空冒出\"电视\"。所以这个空要补一句\"这种金字塔之所以延续，原因之一在于……电视\"，既解释金字塔、又把下段的\"电视\"引出来。\nthis pyramid of production 回指+首引 television+因果承接，全中 F 逐条对上：① One reason for the persistence of this pyramid of production 中 this pyramid of production 直接回指 a pyramid of production remains；② One reason 提供\"延续之原因\"的因果逻辑；③ defined by a single medium – television – and television is defined by downloading 首次点名 television，为下段 Television is a one-way tap 完美铺路。上接金字塔、下引电视，双向缝合。","options":{},"choiceEn":"One reason for the persistence of this pyramid of production is that for the past half-century, much of the world's media culture has been defined by a single medium – television – and television is defined by downloading.","clues":["词汇复现 正确句须复现 pyramid of production，并首次引入 television 空前 a pyramid of production remains 给出\"金字塔\"这个独特意象，正确句若用 this pyramid of production 回指即严丝合缝；同时空后段 Television 凭空出现，正确句须首次点名 television 为其铺路。","逻辑连接 须给出金字塔延续的原因 空前只陈述了\"金字塔仍在\"这一现象，未解释成因；正确句应以\"原因之一是……\"的因果逻辑承接，把病根指向某个媒介(下段揭晓是电视)。"]}},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Of course, it is precisely these superfluous things that define human culture and ultimately what it is to be human. Downloading and consuming culture requires great skills, but failing to move beyond downloading is to strip oneself of a defining constituent of humanity."},{"key":"B","text":"Applications like tumblr.com, which allow users to combine pictures, words and other media in creative ways and then share them, have the potential to add stickiness by amusing, entertaining and enlightening others."},{"key":"C","text":"Not only did they develop such a device, but by the turn of the millennium they had also managed to embed it in a worldwide system accessed by billions of people every day."},{"key":"D","text":"This is because the networked computer has sparked a secret war between downloading and uploading – between passive consumption and active creation – whose outcome will shape our collective future in ways we can only begin to imagine."},{"key":"E","text":"The challenge the computer mounts to television thus bears little similarity to one format being replaced by another in the manner of record players being replaced by CD players."},{"key":"F","text":"One reason for the persistence of this pyramid of production is that for the past half-century, much of the world's media culture has been defined by a single medium – television – and television is defined by downloading."},{"key":"G","text":"The networked computer offers the first chance in 50 years to reverse the flow, to encourage thoughtful downloading and, even more importantly, meaningful uploading."}],"answer":"G","explanation":{"answer":"G","type":"段末","stemZh":"45. (45)____","reason":"The networked computer offers the first chance in 50 years to reverse the flow, to encourage thoughtful downloading and, even more importantly, meaningful uploading. 联网计算机提供了50年来第一次扭转这种流向的机会,鼓励有思想的下载,更重要的是,鼓励有意义的上传。\n由\"电视单向\"转折到\"计算机带来出路\"，并引出 meaningful uploading 空前两句把电视写成纯被动：Television is a one-way tap flowing into our homes. 与 The hardest task that television asks of anyone is to turn the power off after he has turned it on.——电视只会单向灌输。空 45 独占段末，第 8 段开头是 What counts as meaningful uploading?——突然问\"什么算有意义的上传\"。所以这个空要补一句\"由破到立\"的转折出路句：相对电视的单向，计算机带来了扭转潮流、鼓励\"有意义上传\"的机会，从而引出下段的 meaningful uploading。\nreverse the flow 转折+首抛 meaningful uploading 供下段设问，双中 G 全中：① offers the first chance in 50 years to reverse the flow 的 reverse the flow 正与上文电视的 one-way tap(单向水流)形成转折对照，由破到立；② even more importantly, meaningful uploading 首次抛出 meaningful uploading，下段 What counts as meaningful uploading? 紧扣此短语发问，词汇复现严丝合缝。上接电视之弊、下引设问，双向缝合。","options":{},"choiceEn":"The networked computer offers the first chance in 50 years to reverse the flow, to encourage thoughtful downloading and, even more importantly, meaningful uploading.","clues":["逻辑连接 须由\"电视单向\"转折到\"出路\" 空前两句把电视定性为彻底被动的单向输出 Television is a one-way tap。正确句应构成转折/对比，把被动的电视与某种能\"扭转\"局面的事物对照，给出积极出路。","词汇复现 正确句须首次抛出 meaningful uploading 空后段开头 What counts as meaningful uploading? 以\"已知\"口吻提问 meaningful uploading，说明该短语已在空里出现过。正确句必须自带 meaningful uploading，下段设问才有所指。"]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"Since the days of Aristotle, a search for universal principles has characterized the scientific enterprise. In some ways, this quest for commonalities defines science. Newton's laws of motion and Darwinian evolution each bind a host of different phenomena into a single explicatory framework."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"(46) In physics, one approach takes this impulse for unification to its extreme, and seeks a theory of everything – a single generative equation for all we see. It is becoming less clear, however, that such a theory would be a simplification, given the dimensions and universes that it might entail. Nonetheless, unification of sorts remains a major goal."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-3","text":"This tendency in the natural sciences has long been evident in the social sciences too. (47) Here, Darwinism seems to offer justification, for if all humans share common origins, it seems reasonable to suppose that cultural diversity could also be traced to more constrained beginnings. Just as the bewildering variety of human courtship rituals might all be considered forms of sexual selection, perhaps the world's languages, music, social and religious customs and even history are governed by universal features. (48) To filter out what is unique from what is shared might enable us to understand how complex cultural behavior arose and what guides it in evolutionary or cognitive terms."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-4","text":"That, at least, is the hope. But a comparative study of linguistic traits published online today supplies a reality check. Russell Gray at the University of Auckland and his colleagues consider the evolution of grammars in the light of two previous attempts to find universality in language."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-5","text":"The most famous of these efforts was initiated by Noam Chomsky, who suggested that humans are born with an innate language-acquisition capacity that dictates a universal grammar. A few generative rules are then sufficient to unfold the entire fundamental structure of a language, which is why children can learn it so quickly."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-6","text":"(49) The second, by Joshua Greenberg, takes a more empirical approach to universality, identifying traits (particularly in word order) shared by many languages, which are considered to represent biases that result from cognitive constraints."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-7","text":"Gray and his colleagues have put them to the test by examining four family trees that between them represent more than 2,000 languages. (50) Chomsky's grammar should show patterns of language change that are independent of the family tree or the pathway tracked through it, whereas Greenbergian universality predicts strong co-dependencies between particular types of word-order relations. Neither of these patterns is borne out by the analysis, suggesting that the structures of the languages are lineage-specific and not governed by universals."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"In physics, one approach takes this impulse for unification to its extreme, and seeks a theory of everything – a single generative equation for all we see.","refZh":"在物理学中，有一种研究路径把这种追求（科学）统一的冲动推向了极致，试图寻求一种万物之理——也就是能用一个方程式来解释我们所见到的一切现象。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"In physics,","lit":"在物理学中，","role":"（地点/领域状语）","note":""},{"en":"one approach takes this impulse for unification to its extreme,","lit":"一种方法把这种追求统一的冲动推到了极致，","role":"（主干（主谓宾+宾补结构 take sth to its extreme））","note":"难点： this impulse for unification 必须回指还原 this impulse 是跨句代词，必须回到 a search for universal principles has characterized the scientific enterprise 与 this quest for commonalities defines science 才看得出它指代的是『科学界一贯追求普遍原理／寻找共性』。直接译『这种冲动』是不及格的——要补出『追求统一／寻求普遍原理』的内容。另外 take...to its extreme 是固定搭配，意为『把……推到极致 / 推向极端』，不能拆开直译为『带到它的极端』。"},{"en":"and seeks a theory of everything","lit":"并寻求一种万物之理（一种能解释一切的理论），","role":"（主干并列谓语）","note":"难点： a theory of everything 是物理学术语 a theory of everything 在物理学里是固定术语『万物理论／终极理论』，专指能用单一框架解释所有物理现象的统一理论。此处既可音译加注释，也可意译为『一种万物之理／能解释一切的理论』。直译『一个关于一切事物的理论』也勉强通，但要让人读得出『统一』的味道。"},{"en":"– a single generative equation for all we see.","lit":"——一个能生成我们所见一切（现象）的方程。","role":"（破折号引出的同位语，对 a theory of everything 作进一步说明）","note":"难点： 破折号是同位语解释，all we see 是省略关系词的定语从句 破折号在英文里常引出『换种说法再解释一遍』，译成中文时保留破折号或用『也就是』衔接都可。a single generative equation 直译为『一个生成性方程／一个能生成（一切）的单一方程』；for all we see 中 all (that) we see 省了关系代词 that，意为『我们所看到的一切（现象）』，不能漏译『单一 / single』和『所有现象 / all we see』这两个采分点细节。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"Here, Darwinism seems to offer justification, for if all humans share common origins, it seems reasonable to suppose that cultural diversity could also be traced to more constrained beginnings.","refZh":"在社会科学领域，达尔文主义似乎为此提供了依据；因为如果所有人类都有共同的起源，那么似乎有理由认为，文化的多样性也可以追溯到为数更少（更为有限）的源头。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Here,","lit":"在这里（在社会科学领域），","role":"（地点状语（指代上文『社会科学领域』））","note":"难点： Here 是跨句指代，需补出『社会科学领域』 Here 不是物理空间『这里』，而是回指上文 This tendency in the natural sciences has long been evident in the social sciences too，意为『在社会科学（这一领域）里』。直接译『这里』中文读者会一头雾水，必须补出社会科学这一语境。"},{"en":"Darwinism seems to offer justification,","lit":"达尔文主义似乎提供了（这样做的）依据，","role":"（主干（主谓宾））","note":"难点： justification 译作『依据 / 理由 / 合理性证明』 justification 在此不是『辩护』而是『（为某种做法提供的）理由／依据／合理性』，是『为什么这样做是合理的』。译『辩护』偏法律语境，不贴本句的学术语境。"},{"en":"for if all humans share common origins,","lit":"因为如果所有人类都有共同的起源，","role":"（原因状语从句（for 引导）+ 嵌套条件状语从句（if 引导））","note":"难点： for 是连词『因为』，不是介词 句中 for 紧跟一个完整的句子（if all humans share common origins...），是连词，等同于 because，意为『因为』。容易被主体考生当作介词翻译，导致整句结构错乱。译时直接译成『因为』即可。"},{"en":"it seems reasonable to suppose that cultural diversity could also be traced to more constrained beginnings.","lit":"那么似乎有理由认为，文化的多样性也可以追溯到更为有限的起源。","role":"（主句（it 形式主语 + 真正主语 to suppose that...））","note":"难点： it 是形式主语，be traced to 与 more constrained beginnings 都是采分点 it seems reasonable to suppose that... 是『it 形式主语 + 真正主语不定式 + that 宾语从句』结构，译时省略 it，直接译『似乎有理由认为……／认为……似乎是合理的』。be traced to 译作『可以追溯到 / 可以归因于』；more constrained beginnings 中的 constrained 是熟词僻义，不是『被约束的』，而是『有限的／受限的／为数不多的』，与 common origins 呼应，意为『为数有限的起源』。漏译『更／more』或译错 constrained 都会扣分。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"To filter out what is unique from what is shared might enable us to understand how complex cultural behavior arose and what guides it in evolutionary or cognitive terms.","refZh":"把（文化现象中）独有的部分从共有的部分里筛选出来，或许能让我们理解：复杂的文化行为是如何产生的，以及从进化或认知的角度来看，是什么在引导着它。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"To filter out what is unique from what is shared","lit":"把（文化现象中）独有的东西从共有的东西里筛出来","role":"（不定式短语作主语（含两个 what 宾语从句））","note":"难点： filter out A from B 的方向不能反，两个 what 是名词性从句 filter out A from B = 把 A 从 B 中筛出 / 滤出，译时方向必须保留：被筛出的是 unique，背景是 shared。两个 what 不是疑问词『什么』，而是名词性从句『……的东西／……的部分』。结合上文 perhaps the world's languages, music, social and religious customs and even history are governed by universal features，可补出『（文化现象中）独有的部分／共有的部分』，让中文更清晰。"},{"en":"might enable us to understand","lit":"或许能使我们理解","role":"（主干（情态动词 + 谓语 + 宾补结构 enable sb to do））","note":"难点： might 是情态动词『或许 / 可能』，enable us to 不要译『使能』 might 在此不是过去式，而是情态动词表推测『或许、可能』，不能漏译。enable us to do 是固定搭配『使我们能够做……』，常按『让我们／使我们能够』译，比死译『使能』自然。"},{"en":"how complex cultural behavior arose","lit":"复杂的文化行为是如何产生的","role":"（宾语从句一（how 引导））","note":"难点： arose 是 arise 的过去式『出现 / 产生』 arose 是不规则动词 arise（出现、产生、兴起）的过去式，主体考生容易认成 rise 的过去式『升起』。在文化语境下译『产生／出现／兴起』均可。"},{"en":"and what guides it in evolutionary or cognitive terms.","lit":"以及在进化或认知层面上是什么在引导它","role":"（宾语从句二（what 引导，与上一从句并列）+ 介词短语方式状语）","note":"难点： it 回指 complex cultural behavior，in...terms 是固定搭配 what 是从句主语『什么』；it 在本句内回指 complex cultural behavior，译时建议补出『（文化行为）』或保留『它』但确保上下文清楚。in evolutionary or cognitive terms 是固定搭配『从进化或认知（的角度／层面）来看』，不能直译为『在进化或认知的术语里』。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"The second, by Joshua Greenberg, takes a more empirical approach to universality, identifying traits (particularly in word order) shared by many languages, which are considered to represent biases that result from cognitive constraints.","refZh":"由 Joshua Greenberg 提出的第二种尝试，采取了一种更注重经验观察的方法来研究语言的普遍性：它识别出（尤其在词序上）许多语言所共有的一些特征，而这些特征被认为代表了源自人类认知限制的某种（普遍）倾向。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"The second, by Joshua Greenberg,","lit":"第二种（尝试），由 Joshua Greenberg 提出，","role":"（主语 + 插入语（介词短语作后置定语））","note":"难点： The second 必须补出『种尝试』，by Greenberg 是『由……提出』 The second 是序数指代，回到 two previous attempts to find universality in language 与 The most famous of these efforts was initiated by Noam Chomsky 可知，The second = 第二种（探索语言普遍性的）尝试／努力。直接译『第二个』中文读者不知道是什么的第二个，必须补出『种尝试／种研究／种探索』。by Joshua Greenberg 是介词短语作后置定语，等同于『由 Joshua Greenberg 提出（的）』，作插入语处理。"},{"en":"takes a more empirical approach to universality,","lit":"采取了一种更为经验性（注重经验）的方法来研究普遍性，","role":"（主干谓语（take...approach to... 是搭配））","note":"难点： take an approach to sth = 采取……方法来研究 / 处理某事 take a ... approach to sth 是固定搭配，意为『采取……（一种）方法来处理／研究某事』，不能拆开译『拿走一个方法』。empirical 在科研语境里专指『基于经验观察的（与纯理论 / 思辨相对）』，译『经验性的／实证的』均可。universality 在本文统一指『（语言的）普遍性』，与 a universal grammar 中的 universal 同源，要译得呼应。"},{"en":"identifying traits (particularly in word order) shared by many languages,","lit":"识别出（尤其是在词序方面）许多语言所共有的特征，","role":"（现在分词作伴随状语，含括号插入语 + 过去分词作后置定语）","note":"难点： identifying 是分词状语，shared by 是后置定语 identifying...是 -ing 分词短语作伴随状语，表示与主干谓语同时发生的动作，可译为『（同时）识别出／找出』。括号里的 particularly in word order 是插入语，可加破折号或括号在中文里保留，译为『尤其在词序方面』。shared by many languages 是过去分词短语作 traits 的后置定语，意为『许多语言所共有的（特征）』，译时按汉语习惯前移到 traits 前。"},{"en":"which are considered to represent biases that result from cognitive constraints.","lit":"这些（特征）被认为代表着源于认知限制的某种偏好（倾向），","role":"（非限制性定语从句（修饰 traits）+ 嵌套 that 定语从句（修饰 biases））","note":"难点： which 指代 traits，biases 在此是中性的『倾向』，result from = 源于 which 是非限制性定语从句的关系代词，指代前面的 traits（特征），译时可重起一句『（这些特征）……』。be considered to do = 被认为／被视为做某事。biases 不是日常的『偏见／成见』，在认知科学语境里是中性术语『（认知）偏好／倾向』，译『偏见』会带贬义、失真。that result from cognitive constraints 是 that 引导的定语从句修饰 biases，意为『（这种倾向）源于认知（上的）限制／约束』，前移译作『源于认知限制的（偏好）』。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"Chomsky's grammar should show patterns of language change that are independent of the family tree or the pathway tracked through it, whereas Greenbergian universality predicts strong co-dependencies between particular types of word-order relations.","refZh":"（按理论预期）乔姆斯基的（普遍）语法应当呈现出这样一些语言变化的模式：它们独立于（语言）谱系树以及在该谱系树中所追踪到的（演化）路径；而格林伯格（式）的语言普遍性则预言：在特定类型的词序关系之间存在着强烈的相互依赖关系。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Chomsky's grammar should show patterns of language change","lit":"乔姆斯基（提出）的（普遍）语法应当呈现出语言变化的模式，","role":"（主句一·主干（主谓宾））","note":"难点： should 表预期『应当 / 应该』，grammar 在本文是术语『普遍语法』 Chomsky's grammar 不是字面的『乔姆斯基的语法书』，结合上文 a universal grammar 可知，它特指乔姆斯基理论中的『（先天的）普遍语法』，译时建议补出『（普遍）语法』。should 在科学论述里常表『（按理论）应当／应该（呈现出）』的预期，不要译『必须』。patterns of language change 直译『语言变化的模式／规律』即可。"},{"en":"that are independent of the family tree or the pathway tracked through it,","lit":"（这些模式）独立于（语言）谱系树以及在谱系树中所追踪的路径，","role":"（that 引导定语从句（修饰 patterns））","note":"难点： be independent of = 不受……影响，it 回指 the family tree be independent of sth = 独立于／不受……影响／与……无关，本处译『独立于／不依赖于』均可。family tree 在语言学里专指『（语言）谱系树／家族树』，结合 Gray and his colleagues have put them to the test by examining four family trees that between them represent more than 2,000 languages 可锁定此义。tracked through it 中的 it 回指 the family tree，过去分词短语作 the pathway 的后置定语，意为『在（语言）谱系树中追踪到的路径』，须前移到 the pathway 之前。"},{"en":"whereas Greenbergian universality predicts strong co-dependencies","lit":"而格林伯格（式的语言）普遍性则预言（语言之间）存在强烈的相互依赖关系，","role":"（主句二·让步/对比连词 whereas 引出，主谓宾结构）","note":"难点： whereas = 然而 / 而（表对比，不是『鉴于』），co-dependencies = 相互依赖 whereas 在书面语里就是『然而／而』，表前后两种观点的对比，不能译成法律文件里的『鉴于』。Greenbergian universality 是『格林伯格（式）的（语言）普遍性』，与 identifying traits (particularly in word order) shared by many languages 提出的观点对应，术语要前后一致。predicts 是『预言／预测』，含『按该理论应当出现』之意。co-dependencies 中的前缀 co- 表『共同／相互』，译『共变性／相互依赖（关系）』均可。"},{"en":"between particular types of word-order relations.","lit":"（这种相互依赖关系存在）于特定类型的词序关系之间。","role":"（介词短语作 co-dependencies 的后置定语）","note":"难点： between... 是后置定语，前移译『……之间的（相互依赖）』 between particular types of word-order relations 作 co-dependencies 的后置定语，按汉语习惯前移到 co-dependencies 前译为『特定类型的词序关系之间（的强烈相互依赖）』。particular 不漏译『特定的／某些特定的』，否则采分点会丢。word-order 是固定术语『词序』，不要拆开译。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: Some international students are coming to your university. Write them an email in the name of the Students’ Union to 1)extend your welcome and 2)provide some suggestions for their campus life here. You should write about 100 words on ANSWER SHEET 2. Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: Some international students are coming to your university. Write them an email in the name of the Students’ Union to 1)extend your welcome and 2)provide some suggestions for their campus life here. You should write about 100 words on ANSWER SHEET 2. Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"Dear friends, On behalf of the Students' Union, I am writing to extend our warmest welcome to all of you. We are truly delighted that you have chosen to study at our university. To help you settle in quickly, I would like to offer a few suggestions. First, do visit the Academic Affairs Office early to plan your courses. Second, joining a student club is a great way to make friends and learn about local culture. Finally, whenever you meet any difficulty, please feel free to turn to us for help. We sincerely wish you a rewarding and memorable time here. Yours sincerely, Li Ming","translation":"亲爱的朋友们： 我谨代表学生会，向你们各位致以最热烈的欢迎。你们选择来我校学习，我们感到十分高兴。\n为帮助你们尽快安顿下来，我想提几条建议。第一，请尽早前往教务处规划好你们的课程。第二，加入一个学生社团是结交朋友、了解本地文化的好办法。最后，无论遇到任何困难，都请尽管向我们求助。\n我们衷心祝愿你们在这里度过一段充实而难忘的时光。 此致 李明","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"身份句立欢迎","text":"【第 1 段】 身份句立欢迎 。本段用\"称呼＋身份起手\"法：Dear friends 定关系后，用 On behalf of the Students' Union, I am writing to extend our warmest welcome 一句同时亮明学生会身份与欢迎目的，落实了第一个任务点 extend your welcome，再以 We are truly delighted 添温度。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"三点建议落地","text":"【第 2 段】 三点建议落地 。本段用\"分点给可操作建议\"法：过渡句 I would like to offer a few suggestions 引出后，用 First / Second / Finally 给出选课、社团、求助三条能动手做的建议，充分覆盖 provide some suggestions for their campus life here，每条都具体不空。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"祝愿后按令落款","text":"【第 3 段】 祝愿后按令落款 。本段用\"祝愿收尾固定落款\"法：以 We sincerely wish you 收束，再用 Yours sincerely 与落款 Li Ming 结束，严格遵守 Do not sign your own name at the end of the letter, use “Li Ming ” instead 与 Do not write the address，无真名、无地址。"}],"wordCount":105}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following drawing. In your essay you should 1)describe the drawing briefly 2)explain its intended meaning, and 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following drawing. In your essay you should 1)describe the drawing briefly 2)explain its intended meaning, and 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2012-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"这是一幅黑白漫画，两位成年人之间的地上有一个打翻的瓶子，瓶中的液体流了一地，所剩无几","width":"818","height":"643","local":"assets/writing/2012-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is vividly depicted in the cartoon, a bottle has been knocked over on the ground between two adults, with most of its liquid already spilled out. The man on the left, holding his forehead in dismay, sighs \"It's all gone!\", while the one on the right grins broadly and cheers \"Luckily there is still a little left!\" Simple as it is, the drawing conveys a thought-provoking message about attitude. Faced with exactly the same situation, the two men react in totally opposite ways: one is trapped in loss and frustration, whereas the other manages to notice what remains and stays hopeful. This tells us that it is not the circumstance itself but our attitude towards it that shapes how we feel. A positive mindset enables us to find opportunity in difficulty, while a negative one only magnifies our pain. In my view, we should learn to be the man on the right. Life inevitably brings setbacks and losses, yet complaining changes nothing. Therefore, whenever misfortune strikes, we had better focus on what is still left rather than what is gone, so that we can move forward with courage and hope.","translation":"正如漫画生动描绘的那样，两个成年人之间的地上有一个被打翻的瓶子，里面的液体大多已经洒了出来。左边的人手扶额头、一脸沮丧，叹道『全完了！』，而右边的人却咧嘴大笑，欢呼『幸好还剩点儿！』。\n漫画虽简单，却传递了一个发人深省的、关于态度的道理。面对完全相同的处境，两人的反应截然相反：一个被损失和沮丧困住，另一个却注意到剩下的东西、依然满怀希望。这告诉我们，决定我们感受的不是处境本身，而是我们看待它的态度。积极的心态让人于困境中看到机会，消极的心态只会放大痛苦。\n在我看来，我们应当学做右边那个人。人生难免有挫折和损失，但抱怨于事无补。因此，每当不幸来临，我们最好聚焦于尚且剩下的，而非已经失去的，如此才能带着勇气与希望向前走。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"开场客观描述","text":"【第 1 段】 开场客观描述 。首段用 As is vividly depicted in the cartoon 起笔，一句总起交代打翻的瓶子，一句用 while 对照 the man on the left 与 the one on the right 的相反独白，两句说清画面、不掺议论，落实了『两三句客观描述』。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"主题句领起分析","text":"【第 2 段】 主题句领起分析 。第二段以 Simple as it is, the drawing conveys a thought-provoking message about attitude 点破寓意，再用 whereas 拉出两人对比，最后用 it is not the circumstance itself but our attitude 强调句升华成道理，正是『主题句点破再展开』。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"评论加对策收束","text":"【第 3 段】 评论加对策收束 。末段 In my view 亮态度，Therefore 引出 focus on what is still left rather than what is gone 的做法，呼应寓意收尾，落实『亮态度加建议收尾』。"}],"wordCount":191}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 B maintain · 2 A when · 3 B weakened · 4 D accepted · 5 C bound · 6 B subject · 7 D applies · 8 B raise · 9 A line · 10 B as · 11 A so · 12 C upset · 13 C cultivate · 14 D tied · 15 A concepts · 16 C shapes · 17 A dismissed · 18 C address · 19 D accountable · 20 D as a result \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 D · 22 B · 23 A · 24 C · 25 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 C · 27 D · 28 A · 29 D · 30 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 A · 32 B · 33 B · 34 D · 35 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 C · 37 D · 38 B · 39 C · 40 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"选句填空（7选5） Section II Part B （41–45 题） 41 C · 42 D · 43 A · 44 F · 45 G \n（逐题解析见 选句填空（7选5）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":45,"missingSections":[]}};
